"zinc-carbon batteries."
msgstr ""
"Hrst práškového oxidu manganičitého. V přírodě se vyskytuje jako minerál "
"pyrolusit. Používá se při výrobě alkalických a zinko-uhlíkových článků."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "acidic electrolyte paste"
msgid_plural "acidic electrolyte paste"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "acidic electrolyte paste"
msgid ""
"A moisturized mixture of zinc chloride and manganese dioxide, slightly "
"acidic.  It can be used in the production of zinc-carbon batteries."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ferric chloride"
msgid_plural "ferric chloride"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ferric chloride"
msgid ""
"A handful of dark green crystalline powder, with a weak pungent smell similar "
"to that of hydrochloric acid.  Commonly used as a Lewis acid for catalyzing "
"various chemical reactions."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "antimony trichloride"
msgid_plural "antimony trichloride"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "antimony trichloride"
msgid ""
"A handful of soft, colorless powder with a sharp pungent odor, also known as "
"butter of antimony.  It's a catalyst for polymerization, hydrocracking, and "
"chlorination reactions, and has some other niche uses."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "potassium chloride"
msgid_plural "potassium chloride"
msgstr[0] "chlorid draselný"
msgstr[1] "chlorid draselný"
msgstr[2] "chloridu draselného"
msgstr[3] "chlorid draselný"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "potassium chloride"
msgid ""
"A handful of potassium chloride.  Although it occurs naturally in the mineral "
"sylvite, it can be produced as a byproduct of the reaction of saltpeter and "
"hydrochloric acid.  It can be used for making fertilizer, or potassium "
"hydroxide by way of electrolysis."
msgstr ""
"Hrst chloridu draselného. Vyskytuje se v přírodě v minerálu sylvitu a lze jej "
"také získat jako vedlejší produkt reakce ledku a kyseliny chlorovodíkové. Lze "
"ho využít k výrobě hnojiv nebo elektrolýze na hydroxid draselný."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "potassium hydroxide"
msgid_plural "potassium hydroxide"
msgstr[0] "hydroxid draselný"
msgstr[1] "hydroxid draselný"
msgstr[2] "hydroxidu draselného"
msgstr[3] "hydroxid draselný"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "potassium hydroxide"
msgid ""
"A handful of potassium hydroxide.  Commonly called caustic potash, it was "
"mainly used industrially for its caustic nature.  It can be used as an "
"electrolyte in alkaline batteries, among other applications."
msgstr ""
"Hrst hydroxidu draselného. Průmyslově se využíval pro svou vysokou žíravost. "
"Lze ho použít jako elektrolyt v alkalických bateriích, stejně jako pro další "
"věci."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sulfuric acid"
msgid_plural "sulfuric acid"
msgstr[0] "kyselina sírová"
msgstr[1] "kyselina sírová"
msgstr[2] "kyselniny sírové"
msgstr[3] "kyselina sírová"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sulfuric acid"
msgid ""
"Sulfuric acid: viscous, foul-smelling and extremely corrosive, particularly "
"to organic matter and evil clowns.  Although used to prepare a number of "
"chemicals, it is mostly known as battery acid, due to its widest commercial "
"application."
msgstr ""
"Kyselina sírová; hustá, odporně páchnoucí a vysoce žíravá, zvláště pro "
"organickou hmotu a zlé klauny. Používá se k výrobě mnoha různých chemikálií, "
"ale díky jejímu nejrozšířenějšímu využití je známá jako \"bateriová "
"kyselina\"."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hydrochloric acid"
msgid_plural "hydrochloric acid"
msgstr[0] "kyselina chlorovodíková"
msgstr[1] "kyselina chlorovodíková"
msgstr[2] "kyseliny chlorovodíkové"
msgstr[3] "kyselina chlorovodíková"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "hydrochloric acid"
msgid ""
"Hydrochloric acid, also known as muriatic acid.  It is a strong acid that has "
"a distinctive smell, important and frequently used ever since its discovery.  "
"It still has a vast multitude of uses."
msgstr ""
"Kyselina chlorovodíková, také známá jako kyselina solná. Tato silná kyselina "
"s charakteristickým zápachem měla celou řadu využití již od dob svého "
"objevení a nepřebernou spoustu jich má dodnes."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "acetone"
msgid_plural "acetone"
msgstr[0] "aceton"
msgstr[1] "aceton"
msgstr[2] "acetonu"
msgstr[3] "aceton"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "acetone"
msgid ""
"Acetone, best known as the primary constituent of most nail polish removers.  "
"Flammable, and can be easily used for potent homemade explosives, as "
"demonstrated by the terrorist attacks of 2016."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "nitric acid"
msgid_plural "nitric acid"
msgstr[0] "dusičná kyselina"
msgstr[1] "dusičná kyselina"
msgstr[2] "dusičné kyseliny"
msgstr[3] "dusičná kyselina"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "nitric acid"
msgid ""
"Nitric acid, a strong oxidant and an extremely corrosive material.  Mainly "
"used in the production of synthetic fertilizers, for the etching of circuit "
"boards, and in woodworking.  Remains quite useful both for making a vast "
"array of pyrotechnic and explosive agents and as a direct weapon: not many "
"beings enjoy being doused in nitric acid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "chromium oxide"
msgid_plural "chromium oxide"
msgstr[0] "oxid chromitý"
msgstr[1] "oxid chromitý"
msgstr[2] "oxidu chromitého"
msgstr[3] "oxid chromitý"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "chromium oxide"
msgid ""
"A handful of chromium oxide.  This substance, typically known as the only "
"stable green pigment for paints, is also a mild oxidizer, which can be mixed "
"with aluminum powder to make thermite for welding.  If one had access to a "
"CVD machine and a laboratory worth of reagents, they might be able to produce "
"very durable ceramic layers."
msgstr ""
"Hrst oxidu chromitého. Tato látka, běžně známá jako jediné stabilní zelené "
"barvivo pro výrobu barev, je také slabým oxidačním činidlem, které lze "
"smíchat s práškovým hliníkem a získat tak termit pro sváření. Pokud bys měl "
"přístup k přístroji pro chemickou depozici a plnou laboratoř chemikálií, mohl "
"bys s jeho pomocí vyrábět velmi pevné keramické pláty."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "calcium carbide premix"
msgid_plural "calcium carbide premix"
msgstr[0] "směs na karbid"
msgstr[1] "směs na karbid"
msgstr[2] "směs na karbid"
msgstr[3] "směs na karbid"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "calcium carbide premix"
msgid ""
"A powdered mixture of coke and lime ready to be smelted into usable calcium "
"carbide in an arc furnace."
msgstr ""
"Směs práškového koksu a vápna, připravená k výrobě karbidu vápenatého v "
"obloukové peci."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "calcium carbide"
msgid_plural "calcium carbide"
msgstr[0] "carbid vápníku"
msgstr[1] "carbid vápníku"
msgstr[2] "carbidu vápníku"
msgstr[3] "carbid vápníku"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "calcium carbide"
msgid ""
"A handful of calcium carbide, giving off a faint, garlic-like smell.  "
"Commercially, calcium carbide was used for on-the-spot manufacture of "
"acetylene and historically to power acetylene lamps.  If mixed with water and "
"sealed, it will explode with little strength, but with a relatively loud "
"noise that might be useful as a distraction."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "calcium carbonate"
msgid_plural "calcium carbonate"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "calcium carbonate"
msgid ""
"A handful of calcium carbonate powder, typically derived from lime or shells. "
" Useful for a number of roles, such as sugar production, fracking, "
"construction, paint additives and antacid medicine."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "hexamine"
msgid ""
"A handful of waxy hexamine tablets which could be broken up into smaller "
"crumbs if needed.  This ubiquitous fuel was used to start up almost every "
"garden grill, and no 'real' camping trip could do its cooking without it, "
"until the Cataclysm.  Nowadays, it is even more valuable than before, being "
"the key component in the preparation of several military-grade explosives."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"
msgid_plural "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"
msgstr[0] "peroxid vodíku (koncentrovaný)"
msgstr[1] "peroxid vodíku (koncentrovaný)"
msgstr[2] "peroxidu vodíku (koncentrovaného)"
msgstr[3] "peroxid vodíku (koncentrovaný)"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"
msgid ""
"Concentrated hydrogen peroxide is a powerful oxidant, violently decomposing "
"in contact with most reducing agents.  Can be used as rocket fuel or to make "
"high explosives.  Causes severe burns to any organic matter and may ignite it "
"on contact."
msgstr ""
"Koncentrovaný peroxid vodíku je silné oxidační činidlo, které se při kontaktu "
"s redukčními činidly prudce rozkládá. Dá se použít jako raketové palivo a k "
"výrobě vysoce výbušných látek. Na jakémkoliv organickém materiálu způsobí "
"těžké popáleniny a při kontaktu se může vznítit."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "plutonium"
msgid ""
"A chunk of unshielded plutonium.  You should probably get very far away from "
"this, if you enjoy not being irradiated."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "uranium"
msgid ""
"Some uranium.  You should probably get very far away from this, if you enjoy "
"not being irradiated."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ammonium nitrate"
msgid_plural "ammonium nitrate"
msgstr[0] "dusičnan amonný"
msgstr[1] "dusičnan amonný"
msgstr[2] "dusičnan amonný"
msgstr[3] "dusičnan amonný"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ammonium nitrate"
msgid ""
"A handful of ammonium nitrate.  This white, crystalline powder is commonly "
"used as a component of fertilizers and explosives.  Could also be dissolved "
"in water to sharply lower its temperature, but is there any use for this "
"quality in this new world?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ammonium nitrate pellets"
msgid_plural "ammonium nitrate pellets"
msgstr[0] "peletky dusičnanu amonného"
msgstr[1] "peletky dusičnanu amonného"
msgstr[2] "peletky dusičnanu amonného"
msgstr[3] "peletky dusičnanu amonného"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ammonium nitrate pellets"
msgid ""
"A handful of ammonium nitrate pellets.  These pellets are commonly used as a "
"component of fertilizers and explosives.  Could also be dissolved in water to "
"sharply lower its temperature, but is there any use for this quality in this "
"new world?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "saltpeter"
msgid_plural "saltpeter"
msgstr[0] "ledek"
msgstr[1] "ledek"
msgstr[2] "ledek"
msgstr[3] "ledek"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "saltpeter"
msgid ""
"A handful of saltpeter.  Sometimes used as a fertilizer, this ubiquitous "
"nitrate is the principal constituent of black gunpowder and simple rocket "
"propellants, such as rocket candy."
msgstr ""
"Hrst ledku. Někdy se používá jako hnojivo, ale především je tento "
"všudypřítomný nitrát hlavní složkou černého střelného prachu a jednoduchých "
"raketových paliv, například ve směsi s cukrem."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#: data/mods/innawood/mining/furniture_and_terrain/veins.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "niter"
msgid_plural "niter"
msgstr[0] "salnytr"
msgstr[1] "salnytr"
msgstr[2] "salnytr"
msgstr[3] "salnytr"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "niter"
msgid ""
"A large crystal of niter, the mineral form of potassium nitrate.  It can be "
"processed into saltpeter."
msgstr ""
"Veliký krystal salnytru, minerální formy dusičnanu draselného. Lze jej dále "
"zpracovat na ledek."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "aluminum sulfate"
msgid_plural "aluminum sulfate"
msgstr[0] "síran hlinitý"
msgstr[1] "síran hlinitý"
msgstr[2] "síranu hlinitého"
msgstr[3] "síran hlinitý"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "aluminum sulfate"
msgid ""
"Several crystals of aluminum sulfate.  Historically, an agent for purifying "
"water and as molluscicide, due to the fact that it degenerates their slime.  "
"Just before the Cataclysm, its main uses were for adjusting the acidity of "
"soil and as an additive to baking powder.  If mixed with a strong acid, it "
"could be used to saturate soil with aluminum, causing all but the most "
"resistant of plants to wither and die."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "acetic acid"
msgid_plural "acetic acid"
msgstr[0] "kyselina octová"
msgstr[1] "kyselina octová"
msgstr[2] "kyselina octová"
msgstr[3] "kyselina octová"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "acetic acid"
msgid ""
"Concentrated acetic acid, typically used as a chemical reagent and antifungal "
"agent.  Despite its horrid smell, it was used to prepare several types of "
"perfumes, but would making perfume not be too fancy for post-apocalyptic New "
"England?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "formaldehyde"
msgid_plural "formaldehyde"
msgstr[0] "formaldehyd"
msgstr[1] "formaldehyd"
msgstr[2] "formaldehyd"
msgstr[3] "formaldehyd"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "formaldehyde"
msgid ""
"Formaldehyde, here dissolved in water, was widely used before the Cataclysm "
"as a precursor to production of many chemicals and materials and as an "
"embalming agent.  Easily identifiable by its pungent odor.  Terribly toxic, "
"carcinogenic, and volatile."
msgstr ""
"Formaldehyd, zde rozpuštěný ve vodě, se před Kataklyzmatem hojně využíval "
"jako prekurzor při výrobě mnoha chemikálií a materiálů - a také jako "
"balzamovací činidlo. Snadno identifikovatelný podle svého silného zápachu. "
"Strašlivě toxický, karcinogenní a těkavý."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "thermite"
msgid_plural "thermite"
msgstr[0] "termit"
msgstr[1] "termit"
msgstr[2] "termit"
msgstr[3] "termit"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "thermite"
msgid ""
"A handful of silvery-greenish powder, produced by mixing aluminum and "
"chromium oxide.  This mixture, burning at a constant pace and at extremely "
"high temperature, was once used for on-the-spot welding.  Can be used as an "
"incendiary material in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Hrst stříbrozeleného prášku, vzniklého smícháním hliníku a oxidu chromitého. "
"Tato látka hoří konstantní rychlostí a za extrémně vysoké teploty, takže se "
"dříve užívala při sváření. V nouzi ho lze využít jako zápalný materiál."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ANFO"
msgid_plural "ANFO"
msgstr[0] "DAP (amonledková výbušnina)"
msgstr[1] "DAP (amonledková výbušnina)"
msgstr[2] "DAP (amonledková výbušnina)"
msgstr[3] "DAP (amonledková výbušnina)"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ANFO"
msgid ""
"A handful of brownish pellets, made by allowing ammonium nitrate to absorb an "
"organic fuel.  This ammonium nitrate/fuel oil mixture, or ANFO, is a common "
"industrial explosive due to its stability and low price.  Burns fast, but "
"needs an explosive primer to detonate."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "black gunpowder"
msgid_plural "black gunpowder"
msgstr[0] "černý střelný prah"
msgstr[1] "černý střelný prach"
msgstr[2] "černého střelného prachu"
msgstr[3] "černý střelný prach"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "black gunpowder"
msgid ""
"A handful of black gunpowder, a mix of saltpeter, charcoal, and sulfur.  "
"Pretty useless for making modern cartridges, as the soot produced when it "
"burns will quickly clog any firearm, but it could be used to make some "
"vicious bombs."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "RDX"
msgid ""
"Several off-white crystals of RDX, or hexogen: a military-grade, shelf-stable "
"high explosive.  Can be cast into shaped charges, or mixed with scrap to "
"pepper the blast area with high-velocity shrapnel."
msgstr ""
"Několik špinavě bílých krystalků cyklonitu, známého jako RDX nebo hexogen: "
"vysoce výbušné, ale stabilní látky využívané ve vojenství. Lze jej tvarovat "
"do různých náloží nebo smíchat se šrotem; pak pokropí oblast výbuchu "
"vysokorychlostními šrapnely."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "composition B"
msgid_plural "composition B"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "composition B"
msgid ""
"Composition B is an explosive consisting of castable mixtures of RDX and TNT. "
" It is used as the main explosive filling in artillery projectiles, rockets, "
"land mines, hand grenades, and various other munitions."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "HMTD"
msgid_plural "HMTD"
msgstr[0] "HMTD"
msgstr[1] "HMTD"
msgstr[2] "HMTD"
msgstr[3] "HMTD"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "HMTD"
msgid ""
"Hexamine peroxide: this fine, yellowish powder is a powerful primary "
"explosive, used to initiate detonation of more stable explosives, such as "
"RDX.  Relatively stable, but best not store it for too long."
msgstr ""
"Peroxid hexaminu. Tento jemný, nažloutlý prášek je silná iniciační "
"třaskavina, užívaná k odpalování stabilnějších trhavin, například cyklonitu. "
"Je relativně stabilní, ale radši bys ho neměl skladovat moc dlouho."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "APEX"
msgid_plural "APEX"
msgstr[0] "APEX"
msgstr[1] "APEX"
msgstr[2] "APEX"
msgstr[3] "APEX"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "APEX"
msgid ""
"Acetone peroxide: this fine, white crystalline powder is a powerful primary "
"explosive, used to initiate detonation of more stable explosives, such as "
"RDX.  Relatively stable, with a fruit-like smell when pure."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "improvised rocket fuel"
msgid_plural "improvised rocket fuel"
msgstr[0] "inprovizované raketové palivo"
msgstr[1] "improvizované raketové paliva"
msgstr[2] "improvizovaných raketových paliv"
msgstr[3] "improvizované raketové palivo"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "improvised rocket fuel"
msgid ""
"A chunk of a zinc powder-and-sulfur mixture, bound together by superglue, "
"that can be used as an impromptu rocket fuel."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "water purification tablet"
msgid_plural "water purification tablets"
msgstr[0] "vodu čistící tableta"
msgstr[1] "vodu čistící tablety"
msgstr[2] "vodu čistících tablet"
msgstr[3] "vodu čistící tablety"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "water purification tablet"
msgid ""
"Intended for the clarification and disinfection of unsafe drinking water "
"while camping or traveling, this sodium dichloroisocyanurate-based "
"purification tablet removes dangerous contaminants using powerful chemicals.  "
"The label says to use one tablet per liter (4 units of water)."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hickory root"
msgid_plural "hickory roots"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "hickory root"
msgid "A root from a hickory tree.  It has an earthy smell."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hickory nuts"
msgid_plural "hickory nuts"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "hickory nuts"
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a hickory tree, still in their shells."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "pecans"
msgid_plural "pecans"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "pecans"
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a pecan tree, still in their shells."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "pistachios"
msgid_plural "pistachios"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "pistachios"
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a pistachio tree, still in their shells."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "almonds"
msgid_plural "almonds"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

