"that was purpose-built in a laboratory by a group of experts.  Meticulously "
"disassembled.  You can reassemble and plug it into your own power grid to use "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "qualitative filter paper"
msgid_plural "qualitative filter paper"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "qualitative filter paper"
msgid ""
"A piece of filter paper for separating solids from liquids.  This filter "
"paper has a rating of 2 microns, separating more solids out than quantitative "
"filter paper, but the process takes longer.  It's intended to be disposable, "
"but you could probably use it for some time before it's unusable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "quantitative filter paper"
msgid_plural "quantitative filter paper"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "quantitative filter paper"
msgid ""
"A piece of filter paper for separating solids from liquids.  This filter "
"paper has a rating of 20 microns, separating less solids out than qualitative "
"filter paper, but the process is much faster.  It's intended to be "
"disposable, but you could probably use it for some time before it's unusable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "plastic gasket set"
msgid_plural "plastic gasket sets"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "plastic gasket set"
msgid ""
"A set of three plastic gaskets.  They're intended to be single-use, but you "
"could probably use it for some time before they're too worn out to use."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "vacuum pump"
msgid_plural "vacuum pumps"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "vacuum pump"
msgid ""
"A small belt-driven mechanical pump capable of achieving a vacuum of -29.99 "
"hg (50 microns)."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "recovery pump"
msgid_plural "recovery pumps"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "recovery pump"
msgid ""
"A medium-sized vacuum pump designed to recover solvent (hydrocarbons) from "
"extracted essential oils."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "makeshift water electrolyzer"
msgid ""
"A makeshift appliance which decomposes water into oxygen and hydrogen via "
"electrolysis of sodium hydroxide solution.  Much less energy-efficient than "
"actual industrial equipment."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "makeshift ammonia machine reactor"
msgid ""
"A huge appliance built from salvaged industrial equipment, which produces "
"ammonia via the Haber-Bosch process from hydrogen and nitrogen.  As it uses "
"primitive catalysts for the reaction, energy efficiency is very low.  This "
"one is powered by electricity."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "makeshift ammonia machine pipework"
msgid ""
"A rather complicated system of thick-walled pipes, powerful compressors, and "
"wiring, meant to interface with a reactor producing ammonia from nitrogen and "
"hydrogen via Haber-Bosch process.  It also acts as a power source for all the "
"low-powered electrical components of the system."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "makeshift nitrogen generator"
msgid ""
"A large makeshift appliance which captures nitrogen from the air for use in "
"chemistry projects.  It includes a standard air filter for filtering out dust "
"and other large particles, a deliquescent dryer to remove water vapor from "
"air, and a nitrogen membrane filter to separate nitrogen from dry air."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "butane tank"
msgid_plural "tanks of butane"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "butane tank"
msgid ""
"A tank of compressed butane.  Aside from its practicality as fuel, it can "
"also be used to extract essential oils from organic material."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hydrogen tank"
msgid_plural "hydrogen tanks"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "hydrogen tank"
msgid ""
"A tank of compressed hydrogen gas.  If you need to make water from scratch, "
"or lift a zeppelin, it could come in handy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/containers.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/containers.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "pressurized tank"
msgid_plural "pressurized tanks"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "pressurized tank"
msgid "A tank designed to hold high pressure gases."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hygrometer"
msgid_plural "hygrometers"
msgstr[0] "vlhkoměr"
msgstr[1] "vlhkoměrů"
msgstr[2] "vlhkoměrů"
msgstr[3] "vlhkoměr"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "hygrometer"
msgid "A plastic hygrometer that can read the relative humidity in the air."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "nitrogen tank"
msgid_plural "nitrogen tanks"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "nitrogen tank"
msgid ""
"A tank of compressed nitrogen gas.  Nitrogen is useful for its lack of "
"reactivity.  Don't try to breathe it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Magazine name
msgid "oxygen tank"
msgid_plural "oxygen tanks"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of magazine "oxygen tank"
#. ~ Description of "oxygen tank"
msgid ""
"A large steel cylinder used for storing pressurized gas.  It is marked with a "
"faded, but legible O2 symbol."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "platinum grille"
msgid_plural "platinum grilles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "platinum grille"
msgid ""
"A metal grille with a layer of platinum plating, suitable for use as a "
"catalyst for some chemical reactions."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "portal generator"
msgid_plural "portal generators"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "portal generator"
msgid ""
"A rare, bizarre, and arcane device of an otherworldly nature.  It's giving "
"you a headache just looking at it.  It is covered in alien markings."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "teleport pad"
msgid ""
"A kit for a teleporter trap, consisting of a teleporter and a solar cell that "
"is triggered when stepped upon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "teleport pad"
msgid "You place the telepad."
msgstr "Položil jsi telepad."

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "teleporter"
msgid_plural "teleporters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "teleporter"
msgid "An experimental device that will teleport you a short distance when activated."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000"
msgid_plural "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000s"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000"
msgid ""
"A briefcase with a built-in laptop that looks like it's from the 80s.  Its "
"vintage monochrome monitor displays a plethora of meteorological data.  No "
"sign of the FLDSMDFR, however."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "basic laboratory analysis kit"
msgid_plural "basic laboratory analysis kits"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "basic laboratory analysis kit"
msgid ""
"A hefty kit containing some basic things you should probably not try to do "
"precise chemistry without: a small balance scale, a spectrophotometer, a "
"melting point apparatus, a pH meter, and a set of paper for thin layer "
"chromatography.  This makes it a lot easier to feel confident that the "
"chemical you've made is what you think it is."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "small weight scale"
msgid_plural "small weight scales"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "small weight scale"
msgid ""
"A simple scale that uses a set of steel weights on sliding bars to measure a "
"sample's mass quite accurately."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "spectrophotometer"
msgid_plural "spectrophotometers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "spectrophotometer"
msgid ""
"A ubiquitous analytical chemistry tool that measures the light absorption of "
"a liquid sample in a special tube called a cuvette."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "set of spectrometry cuvettes"
msgid_plural "sets of spectrometry cuvettes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "set of spectrometry cuvettes"
msgid ""
"A small box filled with precisely-calibrated square plastic tubes for "
"laboratory spectrometer use."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "pH meter"
msgid_plural "pH meters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "pH meter"
msgid ""
"A pair of glass probes attached to a voltmeter.  By putting one probe into a "
"calibration solution (conveniently included) and the other in a substance, "
"you can calculate the substance's acidity."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "voltmeter"
msgid_plural "voltmeters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "voltmeter"
msgid ""
"A device with two probes that let you measure the electrical potential "
"between two points."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "multimeter"
msgid_plural "multimeters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "multimeter"
msgid ""
"A gadget that is a little bigger than a handheld calculator, with a digital "
"display and two pointed probes connected by wires.  It can measure not just "
"voltage, but current in amps, and resistance in ohms, as well as test for "
"electrical continuity."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "melting point apparatus"
msgid_plural "units of melting point apparatus"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "melting point apparatus"
msgid ""
"A hot plate with a metal housing attached.  The metal housing has a "
"magnification viewport and a slot into which a capillary tube containing a "
"crystallized sample is inserted.  The device lets you precisely measure the "
"melting point of a crystal, a property very useful in identifying what it is "
"and how pure it is."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "vortex device"
msgid_plural "vortex devices"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "vortex device"
msgid ""
"A small, hefty, boring-looking machine.  Its weighted trapezoidal frame has a "
"single on-off switch and a speed dial, and on top of it sits a rubber "
"receptacle.  Pressing a test tube into the receptacle would, with power, "
"rapidly shake and mix the contents of the test tube.  It's surprisingly fun "
"to use."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "light detector"
msgid_plural "light detectors"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "light detector"
msgid ""
"A photodiode on a chip, designed to convert incoming light to electrical "
"energy for quantification."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "glass prism"
msgid_plural "glass prisms"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "glass prism"
msgid "A high-quality crystal glass prism for separating and redirecting light."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "small glass tube"
msgid_plural "small glass tubes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "small glass tube"
msgid "A small glass tube.  Small, tube-shaped, and made of glass."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "microscope"
msgid_plural "microscopes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "microscope"
msgid ""
"A classic tool for the ages!  This hefty, durable piece of lab equipment "
"makes small things look bigger.  Without electricity the light doesn't work, "
"but the rest of it is surprisingly functional.  Unfortunately it's not useful "
"for very much at the moment."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "dissecting microscope"
msgid_plural "dissecting microscopes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "dissecting microscope"
msgid ""
"This microscope has less magnification than a standard one.  It's also "
"stereoscopic and produces a neat 3-D image of the surface.  It was typically "
"used for performing dissections and other fine-detail work on small "
"creatures.  It still works pretty well with an added light source, but what "
"would you do with it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "separation funnel"
msgid_plural "separation funnels"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "separation funnel"
msgid ""
"This thing doesn't look much like a funnel.  It's a teardrop-shaped piece of "
"glass with a stopper at the wide end and a valve at the other.  It can be "
"used to wash one liquid with another, like water and an oil, and then draw "
"off whichever of the two liquids contains a higher amount of whatever "
"compound you're trying to isolate.  With a high level of skill, it can also "
"be used to make juvenile farting noises."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "burette"
msgid_plural "burettes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "burette"
msgid ""
"A tall glass column with a stopcock at the end.  If you're serious about "
"chemistry, you probably have a tattoo of one of these somewhere."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "rotary evaporator"
msgid_plural "rotary evaporators"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "rotary evaporator"
msgid ""
"Just looking at this thing makes you feel like a proper mad scientist.  It's "
"a series of glass tubes and round flasks, connected to a central motor and a "
"heating element.  The heating element warms one flask, kept rotating by the "
"motor, evaporating the contents.  The vapor is then condensed in the tubes "
"and collected in another flask, in case you wanted to save it for later."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fractional distillation apparatus"
msgid_plural "fractional distillation apparatuses"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "fractional distillation apparatus"
msgid ""
"One of the classic pieces of mad science glassware, this is a small-volume "
"still that passes vapor through a fractional distillation column and then "
"condenses the distillate in a cooled collection column.  A grad student or a "
"robot (is there really any difference?) collects the distillate in fractions "
"so that specific contents can be analyzed.  Going a few milliliters at a "
"time, it would not be very effective to try to distill whiskey in this thing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "electrophoresis tray"
msgid_plural "electrophoresis trays"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "electrophoresis tray"
msgid ""
"A set of plastic trays, electrodes, and a power supply designed to create an "
"electric voltage gradient through a liquid solution containing a solid gel.  "
"Stuff like proteins and DNA would then get separated on the gel according to "
"electrical charge and size.  Pretty useless now for anything but salvage."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "microcentrifuge"
msgid_plural "microcentrifuges"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "microcentrifuge"
msgid ""
"A smaller, benchtop version of the larger furniture-sized centrifuge.  Don't "
"be fooled by its portable scale; it's still a very powerful piece of "
"equipment that can spin stuff really quickly.  It's not a toy!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "plastic stopcock"
msgid_plural "plastic stopcocks"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "plastic stopcock"
msgid "Stop giggling.  This is a tiny plastic valve, get your mind out of the gutter."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "test tube rack"
msgid_plural "test tube racks"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "test tube rack"
msgid ""
"A plastic box with holes in it.  Not that exciting, unless you're desperate "
"for a place to store a test tube.  Then it's great."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "microcentrifuge tube tray"
msgid_plural "microcentrifuge tube trays"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "microcentrifuge tube tray"
msgid "A plastic tray riddled with small holes, for storing microcentrifuge tubes."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ring stand"
msgid_plural "ring stands"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "ring stand"
msgid "A heavy metal plate and a sturdy rod, for clamping lab stuff to."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "set of ring stand clamps"
msgid_plural "sets of ring stand clamps"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "set of ring stand clamps"
msgid ""
"A small box with a jumbled assortment of clamps for mounting on ring stands.  "
"There seems to be some sort of rule that all of them are missing at least one "
"wing nut for tightening; twist ties, duct tape, and other random stuff has "
"been used to compensate."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sextant"
msgid_plural "sextants"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "sextant"
msgid ""
"A tool for measuring angles of distant objects.  It can be used for measuring "
"the altitude of the sun."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "lux meter"
msgid_plural "lux meters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#. ~ Description of "lux meter"
msgid "A tool for measuring illuminance."
msgstr ""

