#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ HVAC maintenance.  Keeps melchior from boiling to death and you from
#. choking on stale bunker air.
msgid "Hub 01 HVAC maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Darla_Novak.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ Job description of "Hub 01 HVAC maintenance" NPC class
#. ~ HVAC maintenance.  Keeps melchior from boiling to death and you from
#. choking on stale bunker air.
#. ~ Job description of "Hub 01 Server Maintenance" NPC class
#. ~ HVAC maintenance.  Resident dungeon master.
msgid "I'm part of Hub 01's maintenance crew."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Darla_Novak.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, hey.  The rumors were true, there really is someone new around.  Nice to "
"meet you, call me Darla."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Jonathan Farrier"
msgstr "Jonathan Farrier"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
msgid "assistant"
msgstr "asistent"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Trucker and now general handyman.  Used to work as a cargo driver for a
#. company supplying Hub 01, is only inside the lab by chance.
msgid "Hub 01 Assistant"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#. ~ Job description of "Hub 01 Assistant" NPC class
#. ~ Trucker and now general handyman.  Used to work as a cargo driver for a
#. company supplying Hub 01, is only inside the lab by chance.
msgid "I do miscellaneous jobs within Hub 01."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Aw, hey, you must be that new blood runnin' jobs up top.  So, they finally "
"let you down, eh?  My name's Jon, Jon Farrier.  Nice to meet you, real nice."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Sunil Narayana"
msgstr "Sunil Narayana"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
msgid "server maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ HVAC maintenance.  Resident dungeon master.
msgid "Hub 01 Server Maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oooh, the NEW person.  So, you're not just some rumor they cooked up as a "
"team building exercise.  I'm Sunil, welcome to the underground."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "the intercom"
msgstr "Intercom"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Refusal reason for a shop item group
msgid "You're not yet qualified to buy this"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Refusal reason for a shop item group
msgid "You need to earn an HWP first"
msgstr "Nejdřív potřebuješ HZP."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Reason for a shopkeeper blacklist entry
msgid "Will not buy back their own gear"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom is silent."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom crackles on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom's red LED blinks on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom says something unintelligible."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&An intercom is embedded into the wall here, just next to the card reader.  "
"It's a metal box about as big as a dinner plate, with a speaker shaped like a "
"downwards curve and a large camera prominently featured in the center.  You "
"see a single metal button with a dark LED next to it.  The intercom is silent."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Identify yourself before the intercom.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Press the button.]"
msgstr "[Zmáčknout tlačítko.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Bang on the metal door.]"
msgstr "[Zabouchat na železné dveře.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello again.  Brought us anything good?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, hi.  Doing okay?"
msgstr "Ale ahoj. Daří se?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How's that armor working?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sorry, I didn't catch that."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "-ello?  Hello?\"  [Thump thump.]  \"Oh, there we go."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The voice on the intercom is humming a tune."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What's up with the interference in this thing?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Speak slowly and clearly.  Please."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Say again?"
msgstr "Zopakuješ to?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So, do you need something?"
msgstr "Takže, potřebuješ něco?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yes, mercenary?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Mercenary."
msgstr "Žoldák."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well?"
msgstr "No?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Say it."
msgstr "Pověz."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Get with it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Make it quick."
msgstr "Zrychli to."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't loiter."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't do anything stupid."
msgstr "Žádné hlouposti."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ugh, I hate intercom duty… oh, um.  Hello."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please don't bother us senselessly."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If/you speak to/understand… you/me. Yes?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's discuss contracts."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything fancier you can sell?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's discuss prototypes."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The traders at the refugee center asked me to deliver this drive of FEMA data…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You mentioned portal storms.  What are those?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Listen, something happened earlier.  The world got… bad.  Things felt very "
"wrong.  Do you know anything about what that was?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have some portal storm recordings."
msgstr "Mám nějaké záznamy na portálové bouře."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have found more of those golden robots, can you make anything of them yet?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What the hell were you testing out there?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your scientist was wearing some kind of armor.  What is it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I found this in the collapsed tower with the other data.  Is it useful to "
"your people?  [Hand over the UHMWPE nanofabricator template.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I saw that your mercs have specialty rifles.  Would I be able to get one of "
"those?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think one of your operatives has vouched for my competency.  I'd like one "
"of those rifles."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, about that protective gear?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You mentioned you had a map of the area?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I need some gear to outfit my crew, I think five sets of police riot armor "
"would do the trick."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm here and I've got the goods."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cost of the armor plus everything left in the tower."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom crackles with static as it turns on.  The LED next to the "
"button lights up a bright red, and the camera lens whirs as it focuses on "
"you.  There is no immediate response."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "…Hello?"
msgstr "... Haló?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Um, can anyone hear me?"
msgstr "Um, slyší mě někdo?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Tap the camera lens.]  Look, I know someone's listening.  What is this place?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"The merchant at the refugee center sent me.  You were looking for a hard "
"drive from them?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About that hard drive…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The traders mentioned you were looking for help."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom hisses.  A voice of indeterminate sex speaks flatly.  \"I don't "
"know who you are or how you got to this location, but we have nothing to gain "
"from one another.  If you have a reason to be here, then please state your "
"business.  Otherwise, please leave the area.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a delivery from the Free Merchants.  You requested a hard drive from "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wait, what?"
msgstr "Počkat, co?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You do realize that the front door is just open?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's the apocalypse out here!  Please just let me in!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just looking for valuables.  Maybe we can trade?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Look, there must be something we can work out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well truth be told, this encounter ain't quite so random."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I promise you, there is nothing you can do for us.  Now leave, before I'm "
"forced to-\"  They stop suddenly.  You hear a short, muffled conversation "
"from the other end.  There's a brief pause.  \"Alright.  We might be able to "
"gain some mutual benefit.  It's a dangerous task, but if you complete it then "
"we would be willing to open up limited trading access."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Risk my neck for the privilege of trading with you?  Maybe another time."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We are listening…\n"
"\n"
"You detect a slight elevation in their voice, with a start you realize they "
"are nervous."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Actually I was just joking.  Our meeting is indeed a fortunate accident but "
"now that I have your attention would you be interested in trading in some "
"goods?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Some mercenaries I met mentioned this place, said its a good place to find "
"some work and possibly some valuable post-apocalyptic gear."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You guys aren't as slick as you think.  You think no one's gonna notice a "
"pristine looking meteorological station in the middle of nowhere with not a "
"potted plant out of place?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not without significantly advanced surveillance tech most of which were "
"either decommissioned or destroyed post cataclysm."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Actually a bunch of high tech dudes HAVE scouted out this place and wanted me "
"to check it out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I am in tight with a bunch of inter-dimensional travellers who observed this "
"base and sent me out to investigate this place."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I see and do you have more information regarding these interested parties?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not really."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Not much actually but I do know they have pretty sweet looking technology as "
"I saw them having advanced machinery everywhere.  Nothing like I've ever seen."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We need more information on these folks, we will be making covert visual "
"contact ourselves but for obvious reasons we can't get inside information "
"without alerting these guys.  That's where you come in…we want you to gather "
"as much information on these people without raising any suspicions and bring "
"it back to us.  Most importantly find who they are and why are they here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right.  I'll be back with the juicy details."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know man sounds kind of dangerous.  What can I expect in return?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Absolutely not, these guys are far more powerful than me and one wrong move "
"will get me killed, besides I'm no rat."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Inter-dimensional travellers you say?  What kind of tech do these beings "
"operate?  And how were you able to communicate with them?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright listen up."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Information doesn't come cheap my friend."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've said more than I ought to have.  I'm leaving."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"They are a race of inter-dimensional beings who call themselves the Exodii.  "
"These guys are more metal than man in my opinion and use automated machinery "
"to do their fighting and heavy lifting.  They do understand English to a "
"certain extent and when talking they use a strange dialect they like to call "
"Anglic."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"They are a race of inter-dimensional beings who call themselves the Exodii "
"and they use a mix of futuristic and ancient technology the latter being "
"mostly due to their last landing place being a ancient battlefield of some "
"sort.  These guys are more metal than man in my opinion and use automated "
"machinery to do their fighting and heavy lifting.  While their choice for "
"personal defense was more along the lines of ancient gear like spears and "
"swords.  They do understand English to a certain extent and when talking they "
"use a strange dialect they like to call Anglic."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"They are a race of inter-dimensional beings who call themselves the Exodii.  "
"These guys are more metal than man in my opinion and use automated machinery "
"to do their fighting and heavy lifting.  They do understand English to a "
"certain extent and when talking they use a strange dialect they like to call "
"Anglic.  They are here to mine this place of any useful metal, gather any "
"tech they deem worth saving and maybe even grab a couple of survivors to join "
"their ranks before they move out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"They are a race of inter-dimensional beings who call themselves the Exodii "
"and they use a mix of futuristic and ancient technology the latter being "
"mostly due to their last landing place being a ancient battlefield of some "
"sort.  These guys are more metal than man in my opinion and use automated "
"machinery to do their fighting and heavy lifting.  However their choice for "
"personal defense was more along the lines of ancient gear like spears and "
"swords.  They do understand English to a certain extent and when talking they "
"use a strange dialect they like to call Anglic.  They are here to mine this "
"place of any useful metal, gather any tech they deem worth saving and maybe "
"even grab a couple of survivors to join their ranks before they move out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thank you for bringing this information to us…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's talk reward."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"No problem, if you ask me to choose between us and cyborg tyrants, you best "
"believe I ain't betraying my race.  It's unnatural you know?  Please let me "
"know if there is anything else I can do for you guys."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"For your services rendered we can either offer you some riot gear armor or "
"the USP 9x19mm pistol with compatible magazines."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds equitable to me be back with that information in a jiff"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's too little for a whole lot of risk.  I'll pass on this."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Deal!  Now listen close."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll take the riot armor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll take the USP."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ah its you.  Mind giving your fellow American information regarding possible "
"terrorist cyborgs?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You know what?  I've changed my mind.  I'll do your dirty work.  Give me some "
"time to chat up these folks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Please… I stopped being an American the moment the government left us to fend "
"for ourselves."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine.  I'll tell you about these inter-dimensional beings."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There is something else that has come up on our side which requires some "
"field agents.  Would you like to hear about it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds like you have work for me?  Count me in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe not right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Right.  Your handling of this situation was exemplary, and it's clear to us "
"that we greatly underestimated our potential for mutual benefit.  If you are "
"interested, we are willing to offer you more work going forward, and all of "
"it will have proper compensation from now on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "And the trading we agreed on?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Certainly.  I've just finished speaking with a certain individual, who has "
"authorized you limited access to a selection of our internal stores.  We will "
"provide you with pay for contracts in the form of tokens to be used as an "
"exchange currency, which you can then trade for goods.  We are also amenable "
"to bartering in exchange for supplies that are currently difficult for us to "
"obtain from outside the facility."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll keep that in mind.  Let's get down to business."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We look forward to working with you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thank you.  This might be of use benefit to us, but we will need at least a "
"day to read the contents of the template.  Please speak with us again once "
"we've had time."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Very well."
msgstr "Dobrá tedy."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see you then."
msgstr "Uvidíme se potom."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom's tray wordlessly slides open."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom erupts into static.  Then, it resolves into a voice.  It clears "
"its throat, then speaks slowly and carefully.  \"Understood.  There is a tray "
"embedded beneath the intercom.  Please place the drive into it.\"  On cue, a "
"small portion of the wall beneath the intercom slides out along rails, "
"revealing a large tray several inches deep.  \"You are welcome to leave "
"afterwards.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Hand over the FEMA data.]"
msgstr "[Předat data FAMU.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hold on, who are you?  And what do you want with the data?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What am I getting out of this?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, forgot to grab the drive.  I'll return with it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ask Gavin."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The tray slides shut.  \"Thank you.\"  The intercom turns off without "
"another word."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh!  Good.  We had written that off as a non-starter.  Just drop it into the "
"tray and we'll bring it in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't have the drive with me right now; I'll give it to you when I have it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thank you.  Was there anything else you needed?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That question has… a complicated answer."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to hear it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Later, then."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Understand that I'm not an expert about this.\"  The voice sighs.  You hear "
"the person on the other side typing on a keyboard for several seconds.  \"I "
"will explain it as best I can, but again, I'm not a professional.  Whatever "
"caused the apocalypse, it… broke something about the way our world works.  "
"I'm sure you've noticed that 'normal' physics don't always apply anymore.  We "
"are, as of right now, uncertain if our models were wrong, or if this is "
"something fundamentally different to our reality.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"From what we've observed, these events are what happen at the peak of a "
"cyclical effect.  This is gross oversimplification, and I don't know the "
"science behind it, but… I guess the simplest way to think of it is that 'our' "
"reality is moving closer and further from this other place, or model, or so "
"on.  Like a yo-yo.  When these two things are closest together, we get portal "
"storms.  Otherwise, things are… I wouldn't say normal, not anymore, but they "
"are as close to normal as we get now.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Reading a footnote here… we're looking to gather data about these storms "
"using a device developed specifically for the purpose.  I'll add that to your "
"contracts list, if you want to know more about it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are there any warning signs?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there any way to stay safe during one?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That sounds pretty bad.  Is this going to get worse?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How can you know all this?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything useful I could find in one of these storms?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you for the information."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"In a way.  In the days and hours leading up to one of these events, you may "
"see things that are obviously out of place, or that don't make sense.  This "
"is most clear during the nighttime, but you can see it during the day, too.  "
"If this happens once, take note of it.  If it happens again, be ready for "
"anything."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes and no.  When something like this is going on, the storm is going to "
"affect you one way or another, but being outside is much more dangerous.  If "
"you can, find a solid shelter.  Stay as far away from the outer walls as you "
"can.  Being underground is probably a good idea.  There are likely "
"undocumented psychological effects; use your best judgment and your common "
"sense."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, it seems likely.  This isn't exactly something we can measure "
"with traditional instruments, but observation has shown that they're not "
"likely to get better.  By far the strongest so far was at the start of the "
"Cataclysm, and while we cannot accurately predict what the future holds, our "
"projections are not optimistic.  I wish I could tell you anything else, but I "
"would advise you get used to seeing them going forward."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We have a vested interest in determining how these events will influence the "
"future of the planet - as should you.  Most of the equipment inside of this "
"facility has remained in working order, and although the Internet no longer "
"exists in a functional way, we still have a plethora of information that was "
"stored locally prior to <the_cataclysm>.  We are monitoring and documenting "
"these portal storms, and we will continue to do so for the foreseeable future."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Potentially.  We recently came into possession of a video taken during the "
"first days of <the_cataclysm> using a home camcorder.  We have ruled out "
"possible tampering, and conclude that the recording is legitimate.  It "
"depicts an entity that appeared to rapidly change shape, but responded "
"especially strongly to human presence.  Eventually, the entity reshaped "
"itself into a small object, which the author of the recording claimed had "
"anomalous properties.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Subsequent entities of this type have failed to manifest during remote "
"observation of the phenomenon.  We hypothesize that, if they do exist at all, "
"they may only appear in response to human presence.  While we consider the "
"hypothesis too dangerous and too uncertain to test using our own resources, "
"we would be eager to hear the results if you attempted to do so yourself."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've been working on specialized gear for potential agents in the field, "
"given the hardware we have available.  Given the risks we've observed from "
"here, it seemed astute.  It seems we still have some work to do."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[INT 10] The pieces seemed warped.  Whatever you're using to reinforce the "
"armor isn't strong enough."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom goes quiet for a moment.  You hear a brief exchange on the "
"other end, and then the microphone squeals as the voice gets closer again.  "
"\"As additional payment for helping resolve the situation, feel free to keep "
"the modular defense system.  The core armor platform is solid, and we have "
"been iterating on supplementary pieces that we would be willing to trade to "
"you.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've always wanted to be a lab rat."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If you say so."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've solved that issue with our more recent prototypes.\"  There is a brief "
"pause.  \"You seem like a good candidate.  We will transfer over the "
"additional pieces to complete that prototype set, with the goal of collecting "
"additional field data.  The core armor platform is solid, and we have been "
"iterating on supplementary pieces we would be willing to trade to you.  Any "
"feedback on their performance would be appreciated."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hopefully it serves me better than the good doctor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We'll see what happens."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It was a modified Wraitheon chassis, with a custom AI.  We'd hoped that it "
"would interact with the outside world for us, but you know how well that "
"went.  That particular line of study is now on hiatus, given that the project "
"lead… well, you know."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We have no other disposable equipment right now.  You'll have to come back in "
"<interval>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "No. Come back in <interval>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What would you like to discuss?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm back from the convoy.  [Hand over the hard case.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm back from LIXA.  [Hand over the data.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I found it.  I found your template.  [Hand over the silicon photonics "
"template.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The weapon worked!  [Hand over the inactive trifacet.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I found the robot, but…  [Hand over the trifacet remains.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Contract: Return to sender]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Contract: Light retrieval]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Contract: Iron Safari]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Contract: Hazard Meteorology]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Contract: Data Retrieval]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I need a new NRE recorder."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any more work for me right now?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Unfortunate, but not unfixable.  As before, we are willing to provide a "
"replacement in exchange for an NRE microphone."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hook me up.  [Hand over the NRE microphone.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What is an NRE microphone, and where can I find it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "On second thought, I'll get back to you on that."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The microphone is a static version of the same device used in the recorder, "
"mounted on a tripod.  The glass ampoule is larger, but should look roughly "
"the same in design.  They may be somewhat scarce given the current state of "
"the world, but I would advise you to look inside of research labs.  Subway "
"lines may be a good place to start."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You fold up the microphone's legs, stuff it awkwardly into the tray, and "
"slide it shut.  A few moments later, it slides open again, revealing a "
"replacement NRE recorder.\n"
"\n"
"\"Try not to lose this one.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Give me a moment to look at your file… here we are.  Valid assignments are "
"turning up empty at the moment.  I'm afraid we have no open contracts for you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Return Field Data"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Return Field Data"
msgid ""
"Investigate a nearby field and return with Dr. Prado and the robot prototype "
"she was testing.  Failing that, retrieve the I/O recorder stored within the "
"robot.  If the robot remains operational, avoid direct confrontation and use "
"EMP grenades to disable it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"One of our scientists recently left the building to perform a field test of a "
"prototype robot, but failed to return.  We have not been able to contact "
"them.  Your job would be to investigate the testing site, and return with her "
"and the prototype.  Failing that, return with the data recorder that was "
"attached to our prototype."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That seems trivial.  Is there a catch?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There is.  If the robot is operational, it's very likely to be hostile and "
"extremely dangerous.  I don't recommend fighting it directly.  Dr. Prado left "
"the building with a handful of EMP grenades.  If you can locate those "
"grenades, use them to disable the prototype instead."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll do it.  Where is the test site?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Extremely dangerous?  What kind of danger should I expect?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll pass on getting killed today, thanks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's built with experimental combat programming and some heavy-duty armor.  "
"Despite the armor, it's pretty nimble, so unless you've got a vehicle don't "
"expect to outrun it.  We decided to hold off on adding long-range weapons "
"until we finished the initial field testing, so if you can keep your "
"distance, you should be safe."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can handle it.  Where is the test site?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I'll pass."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Very close by.\"  The voice lists off some relative coordinates.  \"Good luck."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You're back.  Do you have anything to report?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Your scientist was dead, but I disabled the prototype.  Is this what you were "
"looking for?  [Hand over the prototype I/O recorder.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not yet.  I'll get back to it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom is silent for a few seconds while the tray slides back in.  "
"\"Yes it is.  It's unfortunate that only the data was salvageable, but you "
"have our thanks for returning it nonetheless.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, I've done my part.  What now?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Is \"unfortunate\" how you usually describe someone being eviscerated by a "
"robot?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Dr. Prado knew the risks, and she chose to follow through with the test "
"anyway.  Her death is cause for sadness, and it will affect us, but you "
"didn't even know her.  At least now, something of her work will remain."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The voice hesitates.  \"About that.  Give me a moment.\"  After a pause, you "
"hear muffled back-and-forth conversation.  You can't make out what's being "
"said, but you can make out at least two other distinct voices."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Return to sender"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Return to sender"
msgid ""
"Find the corpse of a Hub 01's AI researcher and retrieve the hard case they "
"brought with them during the evacuation."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"When the portal storms started, the government issued an evacuation order for "
"critical personnel and sent convoys to retrieve them, with our head of AI "
"research among the recalled.  We recently discovered that he died when the "
"convoy transferring him was ambushed in the initial chaos, but his corpse and "
"belongings might remain intact enough to benefit from his research.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We want you to travel to the convoy and locate the body, if possible.  His "
"evacuation protocol included retrieving and storing as much of the data from "
"his facility as possible, to be stored in a code-locked hard case.  If this "
"hard case is present, retrieve it, and bring it back here.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We offer the standard hazard pay of 4 HGC for this contract."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll take it.  Where's the convoy?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What should I expect to go up against?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who was this person, and what do they look like?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What else do you have available?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The convoy was composed of vehicles and personnel from the US Army, and it "
"was heavily armed.  Our surveillance of the area has shown that the majority "
"of the slain military personnel have revived, including one wearing a light "
"combat exoskeleton.  Resistance will be heavy, but if possible, you may be "
"able to locate and retrieve the hard case, then exfiltrate without direct "
"combat as long as you can outpace the undead there.  Otherwise, bring a rifle "
"and plenty of ammo."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Officially speaking, they were a senior DARPA researcher.  Their corpse "
"should stick out; it's likely the only one not wearing camouflage.  That's "
"all you need to know."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It was ambushed on the road.\"  The intercom recites a series of coordinates. "
" \"Report back with the hard case.  If the researcher brought it with him, it "
"will be intact; have no doubt about that."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom's tray slides shut.\n"
"\n"
"\"This is the case; thank you.  Transferring the stipulated amount now.\"  "
"The tray slides back open with your payment.  \"As an additional form of "
"payment, you have been given clearance to receive a map of the area around "
"this site, to assist in your work.  The standing price is 1 HGC; please "
"inform us if you'd like to follow up on that offer going forward."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[PER 8] The original markings on that case had been scratched out.  Who did "
"it really belong to?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm interested in that map."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Light retrieval"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Light retrieval"
msgid ""
"Reach the collapsed tower basement, and search the ruins for a photonic "
"circuitry template.  The intercom warned you about heavy enemy presence, and "
"of the existence of a hazardous environment."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Our facility once sourced advanced photonic circuitry from a nearby robotics "
"manufacturer.  Their building suffered major damage during the portal storms, "
"and collapsed almost entirely.  However, preliminary scouting reveals that "
"the basement prototyping lab likely remains intact.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We ask you to investigate the ruins, and if possible, retrieve a template "
"for the fabrication of said photonic circuitry.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Completion of this contract awards 8 HGC, the standard heightened-hazard "
"rate.  We are also willing to provide you with a set of protective gear at a "
"considerable discount upon acceptance of the contract."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's do this, then.  Transfer the location."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where is this manufacturer?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You mention hazard pay.  What dangers are there?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't believe I'm cleared to-\"  You hear brief chatter.  \"Apologies; I "
"was mistaken.  The manufacturer was, technically speaking, kept secret from "
"the public.  As a result, it operated using an office tower as a front, and "
"was located underground.  An elevator in the back of the building led to the "
"basement, but it was likely destroyed in the damage - as a result, you will "
"need to find a way down yourself.  While there were stairs as well, it's "
"highly likely that they have been destroyed.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We advise bringing a way to safely enter and exit the lower level; a "
"grappling hook would work well for this purpose.  Given the damage, the "
"elevator shaft itself probably remains intact, and would be your likeliest "
"point of entry to the underground portion of the building."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"About that.\"  You hear papers shuffling.  \"Our drones are unable to "
"approach the structure too closely, as a large amount of interference "
"prevents surveillance, but long-distance measurements reveal a high "
"concentration of toxic compounds in the air, as well as densely-clustered "
"heat signatures.  We expect a high concentration of undead, and other dangers "
"are likely."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Toxic compounds?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about these heat signatures."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "\"Other dangers\" is a little vague.  Do you have anything more substantial?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Back to the contract itself…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Correct.  The source of the chemicals is unknown, as is the exact "
"composition; only trace amounts are present in the air itself.  We can, "
"however, extrapolate that something within the ruins is creating highly "
"poisonous emissions.  We do not know how strong these emissions will become, "
"or what form they will take."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"At the moment, their origin is unclear.  The temperature profile of the "
"building is highly unusual, despite the damage, and is much denser than "
"wandering hordes observed through remote scouting.  A large amount of heat "
"consistent with an extremely high density of organisms appears to be "
"emanating from the basement itself.  We are, unfortunately, in the dark about "
"the cause of this density.  We would advise you remain observant and note "
"down any abnormalities."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"To be specific, there have been anomalous readings that we are unable to "
"explain.  Seismic disturbances have been recorded emanating from the ruins, "
"with a magnitude ranging from two to four, and periodic vocalizations have "
"been documented to exceed 150 decibels.  We are uncertain why or how these "
"phenomena are created."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The more I hear about this, the worse it sounds."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Did you have any other concerns?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Your hesitation is understandable.  Unfortunately, we have already taken all "
"possible measures to obtain data and information remotely, but we are unable "
"to develop our understanding further without a physical presence."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Excellent.  Thank you very much.\"  The intercom recites a series of "
"coordinates.  \"Exercise a great deal of caution.  We do not know what the "
"conditions on the ground are like.  Use your best judgment.  As before, we "
"are willing to offer you protective gear, if you would like it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I would like that gear, yes.  Tell me about it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fantastic.\"  The intercom's tray slides shut, and then opens shortly "
"afterwards with your payment.  \"You have our thanks and our payment."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any idea what I just went through?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You certainly gave me a run for my money, I'll say that much."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"As we discussed during acceptance of the contract, we were aware of hazardous "
"ground conditions, but we were unable to deduce further information other "
"than what was available through long-range sensing.  If you would like to "
"provide a description of the hazards present, we are willing to document them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Detail the conditions at the collapsed tower and its basement.  This will "
"advance time by ten minutes.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Let them know how bad that mission REALLY was.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "…Just forget it.  Let's never speak of this again."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Over the course of several minutes, you explain what happened at the ruins: "
"the zombie presence and gigantic tendrils on the surface, and the biological "
"infestation completely taking over the basement, as well as the hostile "
"threats encountered therein.  The voice periodically interjects with "
"questions or statements; the whole time, you hear the sounds of typing on a "
"keyboard.\n"
"\n"
"\"We would like to extend our thanks for your detailed report.  It is clear "
"to us that the threat level present at the manufacturer was far higher than "
"we had originally anticipated, and your performance in the situation was "
"exemplary.  Should you desire further contract work, we will bear these facts "
"in mind, and ensure that the threat prognoses of your future assignments are "
"adequately assessed.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's fine.  At least now we know for the future."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, yeah.  You're welcome."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's never do that again."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom waits patiently."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Description, huh?  Where to begin?  Let's start with the giant mob of zombies "
"that was infesting the building.  Oh, and there were also horrors full of "
"toxic gas that exploded when I got near them or killed one, so I was "
"constantly choking on fumes the whole time."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That makes-"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Oh, but that's not all!  They were coming from a pair of giant fucking "
"tentacles coming out of the ground like a monster movie that were constantly "
"roaring and shaking the whole building, and toxic exploding spiders kept "
"crawling off and shooting poison darts at me until I got away or stopped the "
"tentacles themselves, which wasn't easy because the entire building had come "
"down around them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Stop talking.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What do you mean by-"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Then it took me half an hour to find the way down, because there were holes "
"in the floor everywhere, and when I finally did, I was in the insides of a "
"goddamn flesh pit with flooding up to my ankles, and to complement the "
"innards hanging from the ceiling that I couldn't see through the gas that "
"would throw me ten feet and make me start drowning, there were dozens of "
"people fused together in lumps everywhere, and did I mention the poison gas?  "
"Because they were full of it too, and so everything reeked and it felt like "
"being in a giant fucking intestine full of people."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please slow down-"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"And after ALL THAT, I find your manufacturing lab on the other end of this "
"thing straight out of a fever dream nightmare, and after ALL THAT, I find "
"your photonics, and then I have to get ALL THE WAY out of the ENTIRE "
"ZOMBIE-INFESTED TOWN so I could bring you your stupid fucking template.  Are "
"you happy now?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The voice on the other side of the intercom is silent with disbelief."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"…Uh.  We are- thank you for finding the photonics.  We will, ah, make sure "
"that the threat conditions of your future contracts are adequately assessed.  "
"Um.  Thank you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Iron Safari"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Iron Safari"
msgid ""
"Disable and retrieve the unusual robot by <color_yellow>successfully stunning "
"it with the prototype rifle provided,</color> then <color_yellow>quickly "
"running up and deactivating the robot before it recovers from the "
"stun</color>.  You can keep shooting it while it's stunned to prolong the "
"time until it is active again.  You can intercept the robot indicated by Hub "
"01, or find an inactive robot somewhere else.  <color_yellow>You'll need some "
"experience in electronics or mechanics to disable it</color>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"One of our scout drones spotted a partially-malfunctioning robot of "
"unconventional make while tracking an anomalous radiation spike close by.  We "
"project that much knowledge could be gained from a close examination of this "
"subject, and you would be tasked to retrieve it for us intact.  We will equip "
"you with a prototype rifle and instructions on how to use it and deactivate "
"the robot, if you accept.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"The success of this contract requires that the subject be brought back in "
"an inactive state, and *not* destroyed.  A ruined robot is of no scientific "
"value.  We emphasize that you use the prototype to complete this task; an EMP "
"blast would likely destroy the subject outright.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Completion of this contract awards 2 HGC, and you will be able to keep the "
"prototype and the equipment used to operate it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You've got a deal.  I'll track down your robot."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about this prototype."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What is this robot, and what does it look like?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you'll give me a moment…\"  You hear the sounds of typing.  \"Its working "
"name is the hm12.  It functions similarly to a laser, but is specifically "
"designed to incapacitate robots without harming their internals.  Once a "
"subject is stunned, it can be manually deactivated.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"A shot will only stun the robot if you manage to hit its main sensory "
"array, which will rely on your aim.  After a stunning shot, you might proceed "
"to the deactivation attempts by examining the robot from up close."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We are as of yet uncertain of its origin and purpose.  Its body most closely "
"resembles a pyramid on what we believe are three sets of legs for mobility.  "
"It is lightly armed, and has attacked our cam-spy drones using high-voltage "
"electric discharge.  We theorize that this is most likely for deterrence, and "
"not to cause direct harm.  Nonetheless, we need to emphasize that its full "
"capabilities are unknown, and we do not know how it will react when "
"confronted with a living threat."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Lovely.  Just a moment; we will transfer the prototype and handling "
"procedures, which includes information of its last recorded location.\"\n"
"\n"
"The intercom tray thumps several times as objects are placed into it.  After "
"about a minute, it slides open, revealing a slender weapon that looks a bit "
"like a radar gun, a tool battery, a sheaf of papers in a binder, and a UPS.  "
"\"The hm12 draws power from a connected UPS.  Please remember to bring the "
"specimen back *intact* - battered salvage is of no use to us.  To safely "
"perform the task of deactivation, please review the provided documentation, "
"and pay special attention to the procedures detailed in subsections IV and "
"VII."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom tray quickly slides shut.\n"
"\n"
"\"We expected nothing less.  We hope you found the prototype's performance to "
"be satisfactory.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Will this weapon work on other robots, as well?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"The handling procedures you gave me seemed to predate the Cataclysm.  How "
"long had that robot been here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We believe so; it underwent intensive internal tests on existing and "
"theoretical models before giving it to you.  UGVs, autonomous CROWS units, "
"manhacks, and other robots should all be possible to neutralize by using the "
"weapon, although we advise great caution; the weapon is short-ranged, and was "
"not designed to target distant enemies."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Pardon me.\"  The voice briefly turns away from the microphone and asks "
"something.  \"Very well.  I am cleared to tell you that it appeared near the "
"beginning of the portal storms, and during this time, it was logged and "
"documented.  No attempt was ever made to retrieve it before the government "
"collapsed.  That is all I am able to share with you at this time."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom tray quickly slides shut.  After a pause, the voice on the "
"other end sighs.\n"
"\n"
"\"…we requested that the subject remain intact.  This outcome is… "
"unfortunate.  We will process the specimen, but it is unlikely that it will "
"yield usable information as to its purpose.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"You may keep the prototype.  You are dismissed.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, alright."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Hazard Meteorology"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Hazard Meteorology"
msgid ""
"Use the NRE recorder to collect information during a portal storm event.  "
"You'll need to <color_yellow>stay outside and carry the recorder for around 6 "
"minutes until you hear a sharp beep</color> to collect sufficient data.  "
"Generate a printout by activating the NRE recorder and offer it to Hub 01 to "
"finish the mission."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"As we mentioned before, our research into the portal storm phenomena requires "
"that we obtain additional data to verify our own local measurements.  "
"Recording this data will require you to carry a scientific instrument called "
"an NRE recorder on your person while outside in the storm for around six "
"minutes.  The recording instrument will be provided at no cost if you choose "
"to accept.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We are willing to offer 1 HGC for each standard-length recording.  "
"Higher-quality data may be obtained by collecting more data before printing a "
"report, and as a result, we are willing to provide higher pay for better "
"recordings."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, why not?  Let's do some science."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How does the recorder work?"
msgstr "Jak ten rekordér funguje?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How will I know when I've been outside long enough?"
msgstr "Jak budu vědět, že jsem byl venku dost dlouho?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do I need to physically hold the recorder in my hand?"
msgstr "Musím držet ten rekordér v rukou?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If I lose the recorder or break it, what should I do?"
msgstr "Pokud ten rekordér ztratím nebo rozbiju, co mám dělat?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Once the storm starts, it should be enough to walk outside while carrying the "
"NRE, as the recording requires no particular actions on your part.  Research "
"insist on the fact that you must personally carry the NRE on your person to "
"take accurate measurements, so leaving it outside while you take shelter "
"won't work.  I'd explain the synchronistic relations that demand this, but I "
"didn't really understand that part myself… oh, and you might want to obtain a "
"high-caliber firearm before attempting to take the measurements.  Just in "
"case things start leaking into uhm… prime."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The recorder will beep once it has recorded enough data for a report.  The "
"longer you stay outside, however, the higher the quality and quantity of the "
"data will be.  While you are only expected to obtain the minimum viable "
"report that the NRE can produce, we are willing to offer increased pay for "
"higher-quality recordings."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You do not.  All that is required is that you have it somewhere on your "
"person; it will function equally well inside of a bag as it would in your own "
"hands.  Your preferred method of carrying the instrument will be enough to "
"collect data as long as it is directly carried on your person."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The recorder is not irreplaceable, but it is constructed using delicate "
"components that are now in short supply.  In the event that the device is "
"rendered nonfunctional, we are willing to provide a replacement at an "
"equivalent cost.  Specifically, if you can locate an NRE microphone, which "
"can be located in certain laboratories, then we are willing to provide a "
"replacement recorder in exchange for it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Transferring the recorder now.\"  The intercom tray slides open, revealing a "
"hefty, barebones device and a light battery to accompany it.  \"Please "
"remember to exercise caution; the effects of portal storms on human "
"physiology are poorly understood."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Data Retrieval"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Data Retrieval"
msgid ""
"Reach the LIXA facility, and search the area for anything of interest.  The "
"intercom warned you about a number of undead aboveground, and the high "
"probability of more underground."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"During the Cataclysm, we lost contact with one of our sister sites, LIXA.  "
"Aerial surveillance indicates that the facility's inhabitants are deceased, "
"and beyond the now-zombified security detail, the site should be sparsely "
"populated.  We want you to enter the facility and make a copy of what they "
"were researching on the provided thumb drive.  Additionally, we will be "
"providing you with a keycard that should at the very least get you in the "
"front door.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We're offering a standard 5 HGC for successful retrieval of the data.  If "
"that isn't enough of an incentive, we do have a manifest from before we lost "
"contact with the facility showing a handful of specialized powered suits in "
"inventory.  You are free to take any that are left."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, I'll see if I can't get that data for you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What can you tell me about what they were doing there?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What does LIXA even mean?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If I lose the ID card or the memory stick, what should I do?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"All I can tell you is that they were conducting cutting-edge research related "
"to-\" The intercom abruptly cuts off for several seconds before coming back "
"on, the voice sounding apologetic, \"Sorry, but as it turns out I'm not at "
"liberty to divulge that information.  What I can do however is recommend you "
"bring an NRE recorder with you if you still have one."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's an acronym that stands for Laser Interferometer eXodimensional resonance "
"Assay."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, the ID card wouldn't strictly speaking be necessary if you were to find "
"some way of breaching the facility's security doors.\" The voice pauses for a "
"moment, \"But that said we only have the one ID card, so unless you're "
"confident you can get in without it, please don't lose it.  As for the memory "
"stick I would highly recommend you not lose that as portable drives with the "
"required hardware security modules to interface with secure terminals are in "
"short supply these days.  However there may very well be some on-site for you "
"to scavenge if you're lucky."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Transferring the items now.\"  The intercom tray slides open, revealing an ID "
"card for the facility and what looks like a USB thumb drive.  \"Again: please "
"take care not to lose either of these since we can't exactly make more of "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Detail the conditions at the research facility.  This will advance time by "
"ten minutes.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Let them know how much of a trainwreck THIS one was.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Over the course of several minutes, you calmly detail the events at the "
"facility: the unexpected zombie presence underground, the anomalous nature of "
"the experiment floor, and the encounter with the warped and hostile research "
"staff trapped in the corridor.  Throughout, the voice interjects with "
"questions, the sounds of typing filling the pauses.\n"
"\n"
"\"We appreciate your thorough report,\" the voice finally responds.  \"Your "
"handling of the circumstances was commendable considering the anomalous and "
"unpredictable nature of the facility.  If you seek further contract work, "
"rest assured, we'll take into account the potential for anomalous "
"circumstances in future assignments and relay them accordingly.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Hoo boy, where do I even begin with this one?  Let's start with the fact that "
"your intel was about as useful as a screen door on a submarine!  "
"\"Sparsely-populated,\" my ass!  How did you lot miss the goddamn zombie mosh "
"pit down the open elevator shaft!?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We're sorry but-"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Oh, ho ho ho ho ho no friend you do not get to talk right now.  When I "
"FINALLY got down to the experiment floor, you know what I found?  The entire "
"corridor was turned into a two-dimensional image!  What were they even DOING "
"that turned an entire section of the building INTO A HAUNTED VIDEO GAME "
"PORTAL PAINTING!?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I SAID SHUT UP!  It teleported me to an infinitely looping corridor!  "
"INFINITELY!  LOOPING!  CORRIDOR!  I mean, fuck, you ever see one of those "
"Escher paintings?  It's like that, only you don't just see the surface of "
"what you're looking at, you see EV-ER-Y-THING, and friend let me tell you "
"getting a first-hand look at the inside of my digestive system was *not* "
"pretty.  Oh, and did I mention the light?  Yeah, when some of the laser tubes "
"got broken, they spat out light THAT HURT!  A LOT!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You know why they got broken?  I was fighting the insane remnants of the "
"research staff!  They were climbing the walls, spitting light!  And then "
"there was the corridor itself somehow!  I fought the goddamn building!  I've "
"had nightmares that made more sense than fighting that thing!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Uh… Yeah, sorry.  I'll, um… I'll make a note to try and see if we can't get "
"any better information for your future contracts."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Pay Back The Riot Gear to Hub 01"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I appreciate the credit.  I've got your payment now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have to give it some thought."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "[thanks bro this will be very interesting where's the tower?]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[tell them where scout tower is]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What project would you like to know about?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you decoded the disk?"
msgstr "Už jsi dekódoval ten disk?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[6 HGC] I'd like to buy the rest of the armor set now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to request a Hybrid Weapons Platform."
msgstr "Chtěl bych dát požadavek na Hybridní Zbraňovou Platformu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How goes work on the HWP?"
msgstr "Jak vypadají práce na HZP?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to request a set of armor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How is my ordered armor going?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I would like you to upgrade my modular defense system."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"My phase immersion suit has taken a serious beating.  Could someone repair it "
"for me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "My RM13 combat armor has taken some damage.  Could someone repair it for me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I salvaged this combat exoskeleton.  Do you think you could repair it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How are my armor repairs coming?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've found this piece of XEDRA tech; it seems to offer some kind of "
"protection.  I'm curious what you all can make of it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any progress on the anchor?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any progress on the Hub anchor?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've found a rifle chambered for a caliber I don't recognize.  Do you think "
"you could make an HWP adapter for it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you finished work on that exotic conversion kit?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"At the moment, no.  While you are no doubt proficient, distribution of "
"prototype equipment is so far restricted to trusted field agents.  Were "
"someone else from the organization to vouch for your competency, we may "
"consider extending access."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, Foster gave you quite a recommendation.  Very well - I will authorize "
"you access to our prototype fabrication services for agents in the field.  "
"This includes the Hybrid Weapons Platform, alongside the ability to order "
"spare or replacement parts for your field gear."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Great.  What exactly is this 'Hybrid Weapons Platform', anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Platform is complete.  As a reminder, the HWP will not function as a "
"weapon without a conversion kit installed.  Transferring the requested items "
"now.\"\n"
"\n"
"The tray shakes as several heavy objects are dropped into it, and it slides "
"open.  Inside: the Hybrid Weapons Platform.  On its own, it doesn't look like "
"much; it resembles the body of a service rifle without a stock or barrel, "
"colored in sleek black with blue highlights around the magazine well.  Small "
"yellow arrows and inscriptions are present at certain points, highlighting "
"the fasteners used to assemble the thing in earnest.  Accompanying the "
"Platform itself is a series of four bundles of parts for it, each held "
"together using velcro strips and tagged by caliber.  A drawstring nylon bag, "
"embroidered with the Hub's logo and filled with proprietary tools, completes "
"the whole package.\n"
"\n"
"All in all, not a bad deal.\n"
"\n"
"\"Should you require magazines of any given caliber, we are willing to "
"provide them through standard requisitions.  We hope you find its performance "
"to be satisfactory."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Work is still ongoing.  These things can take time."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'll spare you the marketing pitch.  The Hybrid Weapons Platform - or more "
"commonly the HWP - is a weapons platform capable of supporting multiple "
"calibers via the use of quick-release adapters.  On its own, the platform "
"does nothing; each adapter, however, allows it to chamber and fire a "
"different type of round.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Each new HWP is printed to order.  Materials will require eight HGC up "
"front, and fabrication will take seven days."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[8 HGC] A week is fine."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about the adapters.  Does it come with any?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "A week feels like an eternity these days.  Why the wait?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why should I use this over something like a rifle that doesn't need "
"proprietary parts?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Adapters are standalone conversion kits, and can be swapped in the field "
"without any tools, though it will take a minute or so.  The factory standard "
"includes adapters for the following calibers… 5.56 NATO, 7.62 NATO, 9mm "
"Parabellum, and 12-gauge shotshell.  Two loaded magazines are also provided "
"for each of these calibers, and additional empty magazines can be purchased "
"through trade.  A maintenance kit with the necessary tools to service the "
"Platform is also provided."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"As before, each Platform is made to order.  This is a slow process for "
"several reasons.  First, the parts must be printed to spec; this takes a "
"great degree of precision, and so the process is lengthy.  The remainder of "
"the week is spent running reliability tests as each conversion kit finishes "
"production.  I understand that it isn't an ideal option, but I believe the "
"quality of the product is worth that investment."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I believe the answer to that question to be twofold.  First, a maintenance "
"kit is included with each new Platform that includes the tools required to "
"service it, including a diagram of the weapon's construction.  Second, even "
"if you would prefer to use the weapon only for a specific purpose, we are "
"able to manufacture and provide high-capacity drum magazines far exceeding "
"the capacity of widely-available analogues.  We expect this to be a "
"significant boon to your ability to use the Platform in a variety of "
"environments and situations, as high-capacity magazines can be difficult or "
"dangerous to find in the new world."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Excellent.  Report back in seven days' time, and your Platform will be ready."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Excellent.  We will begin work shortly.  Report back in 24 hours for pickup."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes we have!  The disk contained the configuration necessary to print our "
"armors with a much more resilient composite than was previously available to "
"us, without sacrificing any maneuverability.  As a form of payment, we are "
"willing to provide you with the first functional models of the armor at a "
"good price - six HGC.  While that may seem steep, the materials used are very "
"high-end, and six coins just barely covers the production cost alone.  If you "
"are unwilling or incapable of filling that price now, the offer will remain "
"available indefinitely - just let us know when you'd like it.\n"
"\n"
"\"Should you find anything else of interest in the world, please bring it to "
"us.  We would be happy to collaborate like this again in the future."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not yet.  The contents are very strongly encrypted, so simply pulling the "
"data is impossible.  Work is underway to deduce the correct access key, but "
"even with our facilities, it will take some time."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[6 HGC] Let's see what this armor is capable of."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Understood.  The parts will finish fabrication in 24 hours, once you hand "
"over the stipulated HGC.  Depending on our currently available selection, the "
"price will range from 2 to 4 HGC for non-specialty equipment."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[3 HGC] I'd like to request a replacement Modular Defense System."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[2 HGC] I'd like to request a set of prototype armor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of turnout armor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of ballistic armor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of kinetic armor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[12 HGC] I'd like to request a set of soldier armor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, we've finished printing the requested armor pieces.  Transferring to you "
"now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "The parts are still being printed.  Please be patient."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sweet, thanks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "The repairs and tuneup are complete.  Should be good as new or better."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Certainly; for a fee of ten coins, repairs and adjustments could be completed "
"in two weeks.  We'll also pull suit metrics and haptic data to better "
"understand the situation on the ground.  I'd ask you to make sure everything "
"has been removed from the suit before giving it to us."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The camera starts scanning the armor, after a moment the intercom cracks "
"back to life.  \"This technology is currently not within our database, we can "
"probably repair it but we'll need to reverse-engineer it first.  We estimate "
"the repairs to take around a month and a half, and they'll have an increased "
"fee of 12 coins.  Please make sure everything has been removed from the suit "
"before giving it to us.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[10 HGC] Alright."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[12 HGC] Fine."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, that is within our capabilities.  For ten coins, repairs and adjustments "
"can be completed by tomorrow; we will recharge the internal battery as well.  "
"Please note that if you have made any modifications to the armor, it will be "
"reverted to factory standard as part of the repairs."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Certainly, it'll cost you 10 coins and should be ready in two weeks.  "
"Remember to take off any attachments and batteries before turning it in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"One moment,\" the respondent audibly leaves for a moment and after a short "
"period the intercom cracks with life.  \"We have never attempted repairs on a "
"military exoskeleton, we will have to reverse-engineer it first, expect this "
"to take around a month and a half, it will also cost you 12 coins.  Please "
"make sure to take off any attachments and batteries before turning it in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We will begin work shortly.  Report back in two weeks for pickup."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We will begin work shortly.  Report back in around one and a half months for "
"pickup."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Interesting.  If you could provide us the item, we could direct research on "
"it for a standard work week for a fee of two HGC; after that, we will let you "
"know if any progress has been made and return the item as-is.  Please remove "
"any batteries or other attachments before providing it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[2 HGC, anchor] See you in five days."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've made some notable progress.  The anchor itself appears to provide some "
"degree of protection from extradimensional phenomena, and we believe that we "
"can integrate it into our current modular armor system.  This will, however, "
"make it heavier and less portable.  The armor will remain wearable outside of "
"metal armor, although it will be a more snug fit than the anchor alone would "
"have been.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We are returning the anchor now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Very well; we will need one coin for materials costs, as well as the anchor "
"itself and the modular defense system you wish to combine it with.  As usual, "
"I encourage you to remove everything from the pockets before handing them "
"over for processing.  We'll need one day for construction and one day to "
"verify efficacy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[1 HGC, anchor, MDS] I'll see you in two days."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The anchor has been integrated into the harness.  Thank you as always for "
"your contributions to our research and technology."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Lovely.  Research will begin within the next few hours."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The combination should be a fairly simple matter.  Return in two days to pick "
"up the finished product."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Excuse me for a moment.\"  The intercom turns off abruptly.  It comes back on "
"after roughly a minute, and when it speaks again, another voice is on the "
"other side, speaking carefully.\n"
"\n"
"\"Yes… the Exodii.  We have yet to make contact, but we are keenly interested "
"in their capabilities and technology.  If you were to provide us with, say, "
"five rounds, in addition to the rifle itself and a magazine suitable for it, "
"we believe we would be able to replicate the parts.  We expect it to take "
"three days of research.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Please note that the requested materials will not be returned, as they are "
"likely to be damaged during research."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 12.3ln, PA md. 68 magazine, PA md. 68] Is this what you need?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 12.3ln, PS md. 71z magazine, PS md. 71z] Is this what you need?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why not contact them directly?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've met them already.  They seem friendly; if you'd like to reach out to "
"them yourself, I'm sure that they could help."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"While the Exodii seem benign, our experience with extradimensional life thus "
"far has been… unpleasant, shall we say, given the current state of the world. "
" We find it wise to approach with an abundance of caution.  We are incapable "
"of knowing the true agenda and capabilities of this group, and we believe "
"that understanding some degree of how they operate will allow us to make "
"contact in a more educated way."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Have you, now?  We are pleased to hear.  However, we still believe that "
"approaching with an excess of wariness is a wise choice.  We feel that it "
"would behoove us to understand more about this group before we approach "
"directly, and so for the time being, understanding more about their "
"general-use technology is our preferred course of action."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Brilliant!!  Just brilliant.  Thank you very much.  Please contact us again "
"in three days.  Thank you!\"\n"
"\n"
"The voice abruptly disconnects.  When the intercom comes back on, it's the "
"original voice again.  \"Was there anything else?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem very… excited about this."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Cataclysm has illuminated hitherto unknown facts about our universe.  The "
"opportunity to research - and perhaps understand - technology from not only "
"another world, but another dimension entirely, is an exceptionally promising "
"field of study.  Now more than ever is our continued delving into this field "
"of study paramount; while our focus has shifted rather abruptly, we believe "
"that if there is ever any chance of understanding or even reversing "
"<the_cataclysm>, it would come from studies like this."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The project was a success!  The ammo is fairly rudimentary, but ultimately "
"proved simple to manufacture, and has lent itself well to large magazines.  "
"We will transfer a copy of the conversion kit in a moment; it is capable of "
"accepting specialized magazines that we have just begun to produce ourselves. "
" Thank you for allowing us this opportunity."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Given the context of your assignment, we are willing to sell you a set of our "
"protective gear - a gas mask and an environmental suit - at a considerable "
"discount.  We will part with it for two exchange coins.\"  The intercom waits "
"expectantly.  \"Actually, hold on, we might not have one in your size…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[2 HGC] Deal!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What will it do for me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have to give it a thought."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What the gas mask does should be obvious; we'll provide you with a cartridge, "
"of course.  The environment suit is full-body, and protects you from water, "
"harmful radiation, and environmental hazards.  It's also rated to protect "
"from electric shocks of up to twelve thousand volts.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Bear in mind that the suit isn't armor.  It will keep you safe from the "
"environment, but it's just Nomex and it won't protect you from anything "
"stronger than a punch.  The modular defense system is designed to fit over "
"it, so I'd urge you to bring them both if fighting is unavoidable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"To assist your operations, we are willing to sell you a map of the local "
"area, as surveyed by our cam-spy drones.  Its standing price is 1 HGC."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[1 HGC] Deal!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Excellent; please deposit the printouts in the intercom's tray.  We'll issue "
"a reward based on the quality of your recordings."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deposit a NRE anomaly printout.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deposit a long NRE printout.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deposit an NRE printout.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deposit a short NRE printout.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That would be all."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Extrapolating trends from these recordings has become difficult.  Research "
"has requested we only accept higher quality data from now on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&\"Thank you.\"  The recording changes hands."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Excellent; this should be enough to work with.  Here's your agreed-upon "
"reward.\"  The tray slides shut, and quickly reopens with your payment.  "
"\"Given your performance and our constant need for new data, you are free to "
"keep the recorder for further use.  We are willing to pay for any future data "
"that you're able to record."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&\"Excellent.\"  The recording changes hands."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Great!  This looks like a very high-quality recording.  Because this data is "
"much better, we are willing to pay five times what we paid for the base data "
"collected.\"  The tray slides shut, and quickly reopens with your payment.  "
"\"Given your performance and our constant need for new data, you are free to "
"keep the recorder for further use.  We are willing to pay for any future data "
"that you're able to record."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fantastic.\"  The recording changes hands.  \"At this rate, we'll have some "
"real results soon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Uh… please allow me a second to check this in.\"  The tray slides shut, and "
"the intercom turns off.  Roughly a minute later, it turns back on.  \"Well, "
"it looks like this is a real treasure trove of information.  In fact, you've "
"made quite an impression on R&D, and probably just saved us a few weeks of "
"research at the least.  They demanded you be given a pretty significant "
"accomplishment bonus, so… well, there you go.\"  The tray slides open, "
"revealing an impressive pile of coins.\n"
"\n"
"\"Given your performance and our constant need for new data, you are free to "
"keep the recorder for further use.  We are willing to pay for any future data "
"that you're able to record."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There is an infinite supply of the stuff but I guess from us you can get it "
"clean and undamaged.  That'll be $400."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[8 HGC] Deal!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm a little tight on funds right now.  Can we work out a buy now pay later "
"deal?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So we'd need a sweeter deal than just the money if we did this."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can pay you what I owe in cash and looted gear."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"If you give me this deal you can have all the alien corpses, their stuff and "
"their tower"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well it might be more interesting than straight gear.  Tell us when it's "
"available for inspection.  We expect you back in 20 days or less."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "20 days then for payment."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Much obliged."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Beautiful; please put them into loading area.  We'll issue a reward depending "
"on what you managed to scavenge."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a broken trifacet.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a broken triakis drone.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a broken monolith.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a broken delta drone.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Drag in broken quadraphract leg.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Drag in broken quadraphract.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a deactivated trifacet.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a deactivated triakis.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a deactivated monolith.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a deactivated delta.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We already have a similar model in better condition but this one is useful as "
"a reference."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We can probably gain some insight from studying this unit, but  it appears "
"seriously damaged."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That is quite a lot of broken metal, let's hope R&D can at least salvage some "
"materials."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We don't need all of your glossy scrap."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We witnessed it as a part of larger construct."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm impressed you managed to drag it inside.  We gonna need to fix the lift "
"after this one."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I believe we already have similar model already but is nice to have more, it "
"will allow us be more active in our research."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh what an interesting piece.  R&D will have a field day with it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I assume you were trying to figure out limits of the hm12.  I guess they are "
"right here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I doubt we can get a lot of information from this drone but thanks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
msgid "scrapper"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Haven't seen another face in quite a while.  Not a living one, at least.  "
"State your business.  Maybe you got some use for some of this scrap metal?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Pleasure to see you again, <name_g>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why stay here of all places?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm looking for a specific, strange building.  I wonder if you've come across "
"it in your travels?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I know I worked in salvage, but I don't remember much else about it.  I just "
"remember finding this place and deciding to stay here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I held a modest job here as a scrap yard worker.  Business was fair "
"most days, but when <the_cataclysm> hit, I decided to head out here.  With "
"all the craziness going on in the cities and whatnot, I decided to just stay "
"here for while.  I figure someone might find a use for the leftover metal "
"lying around, so I started selling it to anyone who passed by."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, this place had some barbed wire, metalworking tools, and plenty of "
"supplies.  I made the walls myself.  I didn't know of anywhere else to go "
"either."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Like I said, I came out here when the dead got pissed off.  This place had "
"some barbed wire, metalworking tools, and plenty of stuff to make weapons out "
"of.  Even the walls are my own making."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Think I could stay here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I'm fine with it.  There's a spare bed in the shed next door for anyone "
"who needs it.  Just don't hog it.  Someone else might come along."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  The scrap trader "
"nods along, listening"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", then shrugs.  \"No, sorry, not ringing any bells.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", then raises one eyebrow.  \"Not making any promises, but I did catch just a "
"glimpse of a weird building one time that might be what you're looking for.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure thing.  I've got a few things on hand.  What'll ya have?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's take a look at your stock."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Anything else you need?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Find anything good?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I have another look?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nope, although I have a really good claim by the river.  Gonna go fetch them "
"soon, be right back in <interval>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, good luck."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgid "Obtain 25 magnetrons in exchange for credit with the scrap merchant."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "I need help…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgid ""
"Since business is increasing around here, I've decided to start selling more "
"specialized metal.  Problem is, I can't separate the metal out.  Fortunately, "
"I found some old schematics on a machine for this sort of thing.  If you "
"could get me 25 magnetrons, I can melt down the sorted stuff into bars.  I "
"can quickly pay you in raw materials."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgid ""
"Magnetrons can be found in microwaves.  An apartment block should have tons "
"of them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgid "Do you have the magnetrons?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgid "Wonderful!  I'll start the smelting as soon as possible."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "That's unfortunate.  I guess I'll do it myself."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
msgid "Obtain 300 lumps of charcoal in exchange for credit with the scrap merchant."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
msgid ""
"That machine I put together is working wonderfully, but the generator is "
"nearly out of juice.  If you could get me 300 lumps of charcoal, I'll pay you "
"however I can."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
msgid ""
"Its fairly simple to make some.  I don't know where you could find any, "
"though."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
msgid "Do you have the charcoal?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "Wonderful!  This should do for a while."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "Obtain 100 solder in exchange for credit with the scrap merchant."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid ""
"That machine I put together needs some repairs on it, but I'm out of solder.  "
"If you could get me about 100 spools, I'll pay you for it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "An electronics store might have some."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "Do you have the solder?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"Establish trade relations between the scrapper and a refugee center, and "
"bring back a writ of the agreement."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"I was out scavenging recently, and I found one of those old evac shelters.  "
"Turns out the computer was still on and had an address for a refugee center.  "
"I figure they might want some spare metal, so I need you to go over there and "
"strike a deal with them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "Establish trade relations between the scrapper and some artisans."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"Business has been booming since you made a deal with that refugee center.  "
"The last caravan that came by here mentioned something about a blacksmith "
"down some old road.  Sounds like another business opportunity, so I need you "
"to go over there and make a deal."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"It should be pretty simple making the contract, but I'd recommend taking a "
"car over there myself."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "What did they say about the agreement?"
msgstr ""

