#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "infinity tree"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "infinity tree"
msgid ""
"Purple-blue shimmers sparkle around the leaves of this small sapling.  New "
"growth seems to spring up in seconds, as if in a timelapse, and yet there "
"never seem to be too many branches.  It's always in equilibrium.  Its strange "
"nature allows you to push it around like furniture.\n"
"\n"
"The power of this tree allows you to produce raw wooden items from material "
"tokens via the crafting menu.\n"
"Just one of these could last forever."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "nearby infinity stone"
msgid_plural "nearby infinity stones"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "infinity stone"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "infinity stone"
msgid ""
"Wisps of iridescent energy spark around this immense stone like miniature "
"fireworks, leaving behind a satisfying showers of pebbles.  Clay and soil "
"shift around its base, erupting in slow motion yet never overflowing.\n"
"\n"
"The power of this stone allows you to produce rocks and natural earthen items "
"from material tokens via the crafting menu.\n"
"Just one of these could last forever."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "nearby infinity ore"
msgid_plural "nearby infinity ores"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "infinity ore"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "infinity ore"
msgid ""
"A roiling, rattling mass of ever-churning metal.  Flares of purple energy arc "
"around the formless pile like electricity, and in their wake, thin metal rods "
"and struts jut out, before disappearing into the half-molten heap which never "
"seems to grow or diminish.  Its strange nature allows you to shift it around "
"like furniture.\n"
"\n"
"The power of this ore allows you to produce raw and basic metal items from "
"material tokens via the crafting menu.\n"
"Just one of these could last forever."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "warped rock"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "warped rock"
msgid ""
"A sparkly-black stone that's glassy smooth to the touch.  Seems "
"indestructible by normal means."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "glzt!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "Warped Autodoc Mk. XXII"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Warped Autodoc Mk. XXII"
msgid ""
"A surgical apparatus used for the installation and removal of bionics.  The "
"term name 'Autodoc' is something of a misnomer, as it can only operate if "
"programmed beforehand, something that a plethora of labels warn against doing "
"without expertise.  Bluish-purple sparks occasionally emit from some of the "
"mechanisms."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "Warped Autodoc Mk. XXXIII"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Warped Autodoc Mk. XXXIII"
msgid ""
"A surgical apparatus used for the installation and removal of bionics.  The "
"term name 'Autodoc' is something of a misnomer, as it can only operate if "
"programmed beforehand, something that a plethora of labels warn against doing "
"without expertise.  Bluish-purple sparks frequently emit from some of the "
"mechanisms, and the entire machine has a faint violet glow."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/island_mapgen.json
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "sky island"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/island_upgrades.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_memorize_island"
msgid "Mapping island for future construction…"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "quickheal pill"
msgid_plural "quickheal pills"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "quickheal pill"
msgid ""
"This pseudomagical pill will heal all your damaged parts, but only if "
"swallowed while on your sanctuary island.  No reason to bring this into the "
"field."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "warped lumberjack's bag"
msgid_plural "warped lumberjack's bags"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "warped lumberjack's bag"
#. ~ Description of "warped excavator's bag"
#. ~ Description of "warped scrapper's bag"
msgid ""
"THIS ITEM HAS BEEN OBSOLETED.  If you have one from an old save, you may "
"continue to use it, but no more may be crafted.  You can deconstruct this for "
"a full refund on warp shards."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "warped excavator's bag"
msgid_plural "warped excavator's bags"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "warped scrapper's bag"
msgid_plural "warped scrapper's bags"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "warped hauler's harness"
msgid_plural "warped hauler's harnesses"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "warped hauler's harness"
msgid ""
"A looped pair of shimmering blue-black straps that can be worn over the "
"shoulders like a harness.  They can snugly fit a single item of nearly any "
"size in comfort, and any burdens carried here feel twice as light.  Ideal for "
"squeezing one more bulky item home through the exit when your hands are "
"already full, or even some container packed full of other items!  Just beware "
"you don't break your back doing it."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "earthbound pill"
msgid_plural "earthbound pills"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "earthbound pill"
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This pseudomagical pill extends the amount of time you can stay earthside by "
"4 pulses, or about 50% of a normal trip.  They're precious, but should help "
"buy time for a difficult extract."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "homeward mote"
msgid_plural "homeward motes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "homeward mote"
msgid ""
"Though visibly little more than a glowing dustbunny, this strange ethereal "
"mote of warp essence reveals, on closer inspection, something more.  A tiny, "
"twisting, half-visible thread of shimmering bluish-purple trails away into "
"the sky and far out of sight, unimpeded by any obstacles.\n"
"\n"
"Taking this rare and valuable artifact with you on an expedition is "
"essentially buying life insurance.  If you die with this mote in your "
"inventory, you will instead be restored to full health and brought home, WITH "
"all items and equipment carried.  But this effect will only last for a single "
"expedition.  Even if you extract safely, any and all motes carried on your "
"person when you return home will be DESTROYED."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ "description" action message of item "homeward mote"
msgid "A hasty escape."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "warped animal carrier"
msgid_plural "warped animal carriers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "warped animal carrier"
msgid ""
"A hand-sized cage with a shimmering portal at its aperture.  Despite being "
"shaped more like a cat carrier, the power of warp enables it to capture "
"creatures far bigger than you.  This may be your best bet for bringing "
"animals home to your island sanctuary.  Activate to capture an adjacent "
"animal, or to release a carried animal."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Autodoc copyplate (inert)"
msgid_plural "Autodoc copyplates (inert)"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "Autodoc copyplate (inert)"
msgid ""
"This strange obsidian-colored plate is capable of mimicking the advanced tech "
"found within a modern Autodoc, and can be used to create a working copy at "
"your sanctuary.  However, it is inert in its current state and must first be "
"imprinted on a working Autodoc.  To do so, find an Autodoc during an "
"expedition and use the construction menu to imprint this plate."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Autodoc copyplate (activated)"
msgid_plural "Autodoc copyplates (activated)"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "Autodoc copyplate (activated)"
msgid ""
"This strange obsidian-colored plate is capable of mimicking the advanced tech "
"found within a modern Autodoc, and can be used to create a working copy at "
"your sanctuary.  It has been successfully activated and can be used as the "
"catalyst to create a new Autodoc at a location of your choosing using the "
"construction menu.  Be aware this cannot be safely moved once placed, and "
"will also require you to add an adjacent couch, then convert it to an Autodoc "
"couch."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "warped autodoc enhancer"
msgid_plural "warped autodoc enhancers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "warped autodoc enhancer"
msgid ""
"A small device, so complex you can't entirely tell what it does.  You can see "
"a miniature chair, a bed, some kind of machine, a computer console, a tangle "
"of mechanical arms, all changing from moment to moment.  When used on an "
"existing autodoc mark XI, you can upgrade it to a more advanced XXII model."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "warped autodoc augmenter"
msgid_plural "warped autodoc augmenters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "warped autodoc augmenter"
msgid ""
"A small device, so complex you can't entirely tell what it does.  You can see "
"a miniature chair, a bed, some kind of machine, a computer console, a tangle "
"of mechanical arms, all changing from moment to moment.  When used on an "
"advanced autodoc mark XXII, you can upgrade it to its most advanced XXXIII "
"form."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "warped grass seeds"
msgid_plural "warped grass seeds"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "warped grass seeds"
msgid ""
"While these are certainly imbued with warp, they don't seem to have any "
"supernatural powers beyond just growing quickly.  A nice option if you want "
"to re-plant grass on your island, for decoration's sake."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wood-floor tokens"
msgid_plural "wood-floor tokens"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "wood-floor tokens"
msgid ""
"A group of small squares of wood, smooth and polished.  You can use them to "
"transform a section of flooring into interlocking wooden planks."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "flagstone tokens"
msgid_plural "flagstone tokens"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "flagstone tokens"
msgid ""
"A group of small stone stones, rough to the touch.  You can use them to "
"transform a section of flooring into mortared flagstones."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sand tokens"
msgid_plural "sand tokens"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "sand tokens"
msgid ""
"A group of small yellow stones, gritty to the touch yet seemingly nothing "
"ever rubs off.  You can use them to transform a section of flooring into fine "
"sand."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "vortex token"
msgid_plural "vortex token"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "vortex token"
msgid ""
"This irregular purplish lump seems to slowly pull in air even while you hold "
"it in your hand.  If you have one with you when you activate the return "
"obelisk and the obelisk is correctly configured, it will drag the entire "
"contents of the room with you back up to your island."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "skyward beacon"
msgid_plural "skyward beacon"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "skyward beacon"
msgid ""
"This smooth purplish sphere seems like it wants to rise right out of your "
"hand.  If you activate it, you will return directly to the island with "
"everything you are carrying."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ "description" action message of item "skyward beacon"
msgid "Return to the sky."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "healing salve"
msgid_plural "healing salves"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Description of "healing salve"
msgid ""
"A lump of purplish goo, smooth but yielding, sculptable like clay.  If you "
"rub it on a wound, it will immediately heal some of the damage you have "
"taken, but the air of the lower world destabilizes its structure and it will "
"only last a single trip to the surface."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Sky_Island/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "flotation stone"
msgid_plural "flotation stone"
msgstr[0] ""
