#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"\"\n"
"\n"
"[TRANSLATE:] \""
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We call ourselves the Exodii, eh?  And other things, but that's good.  This "
"is our home, such as it is.  I'm called Rubik, and I've been assigned to "
"trade with you.  Are you looking to trade?  We're always looking for scrap, "
"metal and more."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That was a good exchange."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's a bit of a surprise, isn't it?  Before we came here, we were in a place "
"about 600 years earlier in time, or so.  We landed in the middle of a war "
"that turned wrong when the dead started joining back in.  Truth be told, not "
"a very unusual situation.  The Enemy makes us fight.  By and by, we came in, "
"and by then the killing fields were ready for us to harvest their bronze.  "
"It's not Avalonian steel, but it's a good strong metal for stopping a "
"nibbling mouth, so we kept some of their armor and weapons to trade."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ah, you've got a discerning eye.  They're the result of many years of work.  "
"We've been fighting the Enemy for a long time, and over the years we've "
"worked out some armor for the job.  Keeps you going a bit longer in the "
"field, if you ask me.  I keep some of the parts in stock, but you'll have to "
"put it together yourself."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This and that, you know.  It's made for a traveling scavenger, you see.  What "
"I mean is, it's well suited to carry around whatever you pick up in the "
"wastelands, without making it too hard to get around nor giving any easy "
"handholds for scrambling arms.  That, and I'd say it's as tough as nails."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's a simple matter of how we teleport.  Our clothes are often made from "
"cloth and hides from wherever we visit, and our teleporter tears living stuff "
"apart here and there when we travel.  Some can be saved if we take care, but "
"there's no room to store nearly enough extra.  That, and our fabricators are "
"always busy, no time to waste on stuff we don't need for ourselves."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"HEH, you can't get enough of old Rubik's merchandise, eh?  Sure as hell, come "
"back in <interval>."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You can surely try.  I'm not the greatest speaker, and I won't just chat "
"forever for free, you know."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, can I ask you something first?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Of course, what can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Business before pleasure.  What do you need?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Give me a second, and I'll bring them here."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Let me see.  Will do what I can for a coin."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"For this one, I can pull out their CBM and give any working to you, or I can "
"just take out broken bits so that they will still be able to use the rest of "
"stuff in them.  Alternatively, why don't you just give them to me?  I surely "
"can help them adjust to life as a cyborg."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This one can't be saved, too much brain rotted.  But I can salvage bits from "
"them or repurpose them for walker, or just cut out rot and neural interface "
"so you can bury them proper."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Lovely!  Benzete (this is a name) is going to be beside themselves, that's "
"for sure.  I mean, they'll be really happy.  This is their first jump, and "
"it's a lucky one."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"As I recall, we were talking about Benzete and how this is a great jump for "
"their first time."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've got to leave the old world before it gets too worn out, you see, and "
"find a nice fresh one on the other side.  Your deadland is as fresh as it "
"gets."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No worries.  I mean, the Enemy is new here, and we have a bit of safe time "
"ahead of us before we have to jump away again."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's a part of it, sure, but this is nice for other reasons, and much "
"better than our last jump.  Otherlands with fusillies and mobbings are really "
"useful to us."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's exactly it!  This is nice for many reasons, and much better than our "
"last jump.  Otherlands with fusillies and mobbings are really useful to us."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, yeah.  Lots of places have different words for those.  A fusilly is a "
"weapon that fires a bullet at high speeds using propellant.  A mobbing is a "
"big metal box that's moved around by an internal explosion.  Do you get it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Great, I'll put that in the dictionary.  Here's a token of my gratitude for "
"your explanation."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They're an otherlander from around three jumps ago, a real optimistic "
"greenhorn.  They're really interested in how we do tracking, you see?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Like an apprentice to the old tracker."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, that word is fine, I think."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, you could say that.  We're from otherlands, most of the time.  Not "
"otherworlds though.  Too risky bringing those monsters into our safe haven."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's a big question.  Otherworlds are how you got those ugly "
"bug-creatures around here, you know?  Walking plants, talking mushroom, stuff "
"like that.  Otherlands are closer related.  I'm from Earth, just a different "
"Earth.  You shouldn't be asking what the Exodii are doing in Earth, because "
"some of us are feeling pretty at home here, I think.  You should be asking "
"what we're doing hanging out in your part of town."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ah.  Home.  That's a long time gone, you know?  Yours isn't too different.  "
"I… don't think I want to talk about it.  I've changed too much between then "
"and now.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I realized that it was a no-brainer question.  There was only one other "
"option, you see, if I didn't join the Exodii."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Robot?  What does that word mean?  Hang on.  …Ah, an automate?  No, I'm as "
"flesh and blood as you are, encased in a shell of metal and wire.  Not as "
"much flesh as there used to be.  The wire is mixed and woven into the flesh, "
"all as one, you see."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's the basic explanation.  A bit of both now, but I used to be just "
"like you."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A junker base, obviously.  A jury-rigged mess.  We'll pack it up and leave "
"eventually."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The otherlands we were in before had only little time left, so we can't say "
"for sure.  But this land is as fresh as it can be."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"To understand how, you've gotta think eleven-dimensionally.  We'll open up a "
"gate and teleport out, the same as we came."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ah, good question.  Enough cybernetic implants can keep someone from coming "
"back as a zombie, but it's not a sure thing.  Some come back anyway, and some "
"just don't have enough cybernetics.  Most of them aren't full Exodii like old "
"Rubik, they're more our friends - like you.  Sooner or later we'll get out "
"there, put them down, and bring their parts back for cleaning."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't think I'm the best to explain that, but I'll do my best.  Our "
"technology might seem pretty high-tech and well made to you, but on the "
"inside I'm still mostly human meat bound up in wires and steel.  Nobody's "
"left that remembers exactly how it all goes, and much of it is cobbled "
"together from a few different dimensions.  It's a miracle they work as well "
"as they do, but somehow it's actually pretty functional.  Still, it can be "
"hard to know exactly what could go wrong.  The ones who come back as zombies, "
"they're generally less well made than me.  Some even did their own cybernetic "
"conversions, and didn't exactly follow best practices."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Faster than you might guess, but it can still take a while, the hardest part "
"is sourcing the materials for one.  We've got printers that make the body, "
"and others that make the tools and equipment the walker will use.  Some of "
"the special parts have to be manufactured by hand, so we have a small team "
"that does that.  Right now, it's very slow, we're still setting up our "
"operations."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know about that.  Each one we make is very important to our "
"operations here, and they're extremely expensive.  I might be able to sell "
"you one later, but not right now.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid " [TRANSLATE: "
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, we're always in need of some help around here.  Here's the list I've "
"got for stuff like this."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "]"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure you can, at least a bit.  I'll do my best to speak your Anglic, but "
"seeing as we're from otherlands and all, it's not that simple."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Same as you, I'd guess.  The Enemy.  The dead."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You want to get religious, eh?  I can't tell you for sure, but the people who "
"claim to know, they talk about the Enemy.  Most folks have a fairy tale like "
"that, I think.  A monster from ancient memory, returned.  I don't know much "
"about that, but something makes those bodies walk and moan, and it doesn't "
"seem to be anything human.  How it gets in, well, that's anyone's guess.  It "
"can come the way we came, through a portal, but it doesn't always.  How it "
"was for your world, I can't tell you."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This is a deadland, you see.  Take a moment and look around, know what I "
"mean?  What's left for you?  The dead will be in the fields, the forests, all "
"over the world.  Anything that walks, they'll make it so it doesn't, and most "
"will come back as undead.  Those that don't, the Enemy will change them as "
"well.  Every deadland is the same.  You've years and more to go, but one way "
"or another, this place is dead.  Though, as far as I can see, you've got "
"quite a few years to go yet."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Spread, yes, through the portals, but we don't know how.  After the world is "
"down to dust, I'm long gone.  Once or twice we've send back a probe to the "
"deadlands we left behind, but none have returned.  As far as I know, there's "
"only one way it goes from here."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you want to try it, I won't stop you.  In fact, I'll sell you equipment "
"that might help."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You do that then.  I'll cheer for you when you stand over the vanquished "
"corpse of the devil himself."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm a lowlife from old Upper Landing, this is my way of talking.  Everyone "
"from where I come from talks like this."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ha!  A new part of our crew.  Signed up early on in the world we were in "
"before.  He's a really tough guy, and the node appreciates his grit.  "
"(Recites some poetry), as it were.  I think he's pretty good as a military "
"commander."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Maybe, but where's the fun in that?  Besides, quoting poetry is one thing, "
"but changing the way I speak all the time takes a lot of practice."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Right.  You see, it's when two compatible people randomly happen into each "
"other and take a liking to one another.  It's a bit of Anglic slang."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That takes me way back.  That's a bit of the old King's Landing right there, "
"you know, calling back from when I was just little.  It… ah, it's really hard "
"for me to think about those old days.  Maybe another time.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Making do, making do, same as you I'd imagine.  Our last home got too dead "
"and putrid around the edges, basically.  It happens to the best of them.  We "
"caught some news that brought us along to your place here, fired up the "
"engines, and boom!  Now, quick as can be, here we are.  We got a good timing "
"this time, seems to me you'd only been dead a few days when we got here.  "
"Freshest corpse I've seen in a while."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're just here to survive, you understand?  Our last world got too overrun "
"with undead.  So, we came to a new world.  This one.  If I'm not mistaken, "
"it's not so long dead around here just yet."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Aside from just having a safe place to live?  We're here to mine, you "
"understand.  Picking the scraps, seeing if this world has any tech worth "
"reverse engineering.  No sense letting good scraps go to waste.  If we're "
"lucky, maybe we'll get some new Exodii before we teleport out.  Pickin' up "
"the pieces of our sweet, shattered dreams, such as they are."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This is a deadland, don't you see?  You've already got an infestation and "
"it's not going away.  There's no cure for the zombies."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It means what it means.  Your land's dead already, it's just still kicking is "
"all."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, we can teleport along as we need to.  We send the scrap along, then the "
"food, and shake off some baddies, you understand.  It's no good for you "
"though, it won't take too much flesh and bone."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Haha, not mostly, mate.  It's not worth risking the side effects, you see?  I "
"keep the parts of me that make me Rubik, but the rest is all solid."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, sure, that's a fair assessment.  I mean, I do get a bit of a laugh out of "
"the look on your face sometimes.  What I'm saying is, if my body were flesh "
"and bone, the device we use to travel around dimensions would rip up the meat "
"and leave me quite a mess.  We can take a bit, but too much… one time, I felt "
"a bit of that, and I'm not in any rush to try it again."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not to me it doesn't.  We didn't get it from around here though.  I bet it "
"looks pretty nice to you."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you've got what I need, I'm happy to call ahead and make the arrangements, "
"for a fee."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh HO!  Well, now you're speaking my language.  We can fix you up good, if "
"you're willing to pay us back.  I'll say it as clearly as I can.  If you help "
"us kill the undead, we can help you get fixed up like us, yeah.  Stuck right "
"into your flesh and bone and wired into your brain.  You understand?  If not, "
"we'll ask the Great Grey to help clear it up."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ah, well.  I'll file that away, so to speak.  Maybe you could bring us a "
"little more trade, and we'll fix you up as soon as possible.  The Exodii "
"won't turn away a willing convert."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"MY accent?  You've obviously never had to listen to yourself talk.  Great "
"Grey has more important work to do, get it?  I have to keep myself useful and "
"keep Great Grey doing what it's supposed to.  Besides, talking to the locals "
"keeps me young and shines my chrome, as I see it."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Great, great, great!  Ha!  We'll fire up the old meat grinder.  Your job is "
"to bring us a bit of good tea.  Not literally 'tea' of course.  That's my "
"Anglic street slang.  I mean the stuff that puts you to sleep for surgery.  "
"The Great Grey says your word for it is 'anesthetic'.  You bring us a "
"thousand units of anesthetic, we'll fix you up with a wire and everything."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Great, great, great!  Ha!  We'll fire up the old meat grinder.  You just come "
"along with old Rubik."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's a fine choice, I understand.  If you change your mind, old Rubik's "
"going to be here for a while.  You'll get to know us better, we'll get to "
"know you better, and that's going to be good all around."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This is what you'd call a 'starter package', if I understand it.  Suitable to "
"get you started, but for the really sweet parts you're going to want what I'm "
"selling.  As we get to know each other better, I'll be able to get access to "
"even more stuff."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/modinfo.json
#. ~ MOD name
msgid "Translate Complex Dialogue"
msgstr ""

